problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106880/ma-source-field/261e2d0231aca4bcdd941284a0e9d0b192d8d759542e5028297ecbaef75bfbfa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106880"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106888/ma-source-field/889a79523939f8ab8b3b47ab9914327299a259f57915e3d3cbf00d8ec2671de1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "6b5db82b-df8d-5504-91e7-fcc98356c581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106888/ma-source-field/889a79523939f8ab8b3b47ab9914327299a259f57915e3d3cbf00d8ec2671de1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "6ba279e7-9cb7-5403-9454-8ad5b15d2a89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106888/ma-source-field/889a79523939f8ab8b3b47ab9914327299a259f57915e3d3cbf00d8ec2671de1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "9cb6755f-48c1-5f6b-9cd2-eb9cbe4c57c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :d