106888" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ the vector space of all $8\\times 8$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{8}(R))={8}^{2}=64.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-106888/ma-source-field/889a79523939f8ab8b3b47ab9914327299a259f57915e3d3cbf00d8ec2671de1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107125/ma-source-field/4d29583a5d7e9f753144f7ee4229cea5b726ec988ba1a9bb5b4dd6885119f6c3/83521de023057e02b98cd57129aff2b19f28e1c5a6f0ec53211e083e7ef0d227" :answer/id #uuid "12647afe-fb4f-5f2b-9326-19bf07c40a1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107125/ma-source-field/4d29583a5d7e9f753144f7ee4229cea5b726ec988ba1a9bb5b4dd6885119f6c3/cd3647f13cdd93f054c3eb2962b71839a156fc1d9bcf1783b918f009045834df" :answer/id #uuid "6e2e45ac-2ae6-5e93-b31c-67cedb5a0fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107125/ma-source-field/4d29583a5d7e9f753144f7ee4229cea5b726ec988ba1a9bb5b4dd6885119f6c3/90329396138dd76fa21a1953e5f1b89ef0e13d51e2cd2fa5527fef40bfc6fd96" :answer/id #uuid "ebd2a414-b8e6-52ba-9a39-7d6bbb93cce4" :answ