" :question/id #uuid "fee906ee-def7-5194-a87e-a1f77108aa56" :question/math-academy-id "q-107125" :question/problem "Simon measures the temperature of the tea in his cup, and the thermometer displays a reading of ${60}^{∘}C.$ After $10$ minutes, Simon repeats the measurement and the thermometer displays a reading of  ${52}^{∘}C.$ To the nearest minute, how long does it take for the tea to decrease its temperature to ${40}^{∘}C$ if the temperature in the room is ${28}^{∘}C?$ \n\n*Hint: You may assume that the temperature $T(t)$ of the tea in Simon's cup decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling, where $T$ is measured in degrees Celsius and $t>0$ is the time, in minutes, since the first measurement.*" :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the inhibited decay equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={28}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-28).\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate our differential equation by separating the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-k\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{dT}{T-28} & =-k\\int dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-28| & =-kt+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this is the solution to an inhibited decay equation, we have $T-28>0$ for all $t>0.$\nNext, we solve for $T(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T-28 & ={e}^{-kt+C} \\\\ T-28 & ={e}^{C}{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T-28 & =K{e}^{-kt} \\\\ T & =28+K{e}^{-kt}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K={e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration. \n\nWe're told that the initial temperature reading was ${60}^{∘}C.$ So, we apply the initial condition $T(0)=60,$ and solve for $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60 & =28+K{e}^{0} \\\\ 60 & =28+K \\\\ K & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following expression for $T(t):$\n\n$$\nT(t)=28+32{e}^{-kt}\n$$\n\nWe're also told that, after $10$ minutes, the thermometer reading is ${52}^{∘}C.$ So, applying the condition $T(10)=52,$ we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}52 & =28+32{e}^{-10k} \\\\ 24 & =32{e}^{-10k} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & ={e}^{-10k} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) & =-10k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the temperature of the tea is ${40}^{∘}C.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({t}_{1}) & =40 \\\\ 28+32{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =40 \\\\ 32{e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =12 \\\\ {e}^{-k{t}_{1}} & =\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ -k{t}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8}) \\\\ {t}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in our value for $k,$ we conclude that the tea will have a temperature of ${40}^{∘}C$ after\n\n$$\n{t}_{1}=\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{8})}{-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})}≈34\\,\\text{min},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107125/ma-source-field/4d29583a5d7e9f753144f7ee4229cea5b726ec988ba1a9bb5b4dd6885119f6c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfe4679b-9724-5502-89d4-05e7661a1b5f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134079 :question/answer-fields 17592186130600] {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "053995d9-9d5a-572e-a184-b3f175a52101" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/72a939d87bda05f6dfa756cbe0aefbe434acc33440f464c6899f2830610d1a37" :answer/id #uuid "f97f4600-e963-5af1-a6e4-9a40da7069c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/43dd586b90042088697b62ed08844fb7d681934fa52e731e3981351603740080" :answer/id #uuid "997b117c-6043-5bde-84a7-173fff6b3502" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/48e4b40a5b1756c2010f2f27fc261ba2e15a38c23c76e446464e77bbd214c207" :answer/id #uuid "852b30a5-50ad-5fdf-b509-9e641d3f9f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/d9a9be2332bbb751f2025845c93c84bd8dcce783d812e2d44aa6f0759066c857" :answer/id #uuid "19b02b38-e01b-595f-bf4f-ccb340e83dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "0208d090-3523-510e-b360-0ef37adf0826" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/72a939d87bda05f6dfa756cbe0aefbe434acc33440f464c6899f2830610d1a37" "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/43dd586b90042088697b62ed08844fb7d681934fa52e731e3981351603740080" "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/48e4b40a5b1756c2010f2f27fc261ba2e15a38c23c76e446464e77bbd214c207" "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/d9a9be2332bbb751f2025845c93c84bd8dcce783d812e2d44aa6f0759066c857"] :answer-field/correct "q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf/72a939d87bda05f6dfa756cbe0aefbe434acc33440f464c6899f2830610d1a37" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "ba1ee846-cfe9-595c-9803-25afded75ec1"] :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & ⋯ & {a}_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108921/ma-source-field/a95b332ba80b3f67f0beb82b30f097a1f4e48da7101da5e0d96dd948bff0ecbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186162290 :question/answer-fields 17592186158912] {:db/id "q-109390/ma-source-field/215e14deff61cd0a869a6ae6d2678e1918ea9cdc3d54a204c6870f26222d835c/5611c708a18a4198a7a9071e80a0f1a03885f349c6a8d22da93e1a69972d1a00" :answer/id #uuid "527df6f9-8e27-5093-a6bf-7c2fb3233e16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109390/ma-source-field/215e14deff61cd0a869a6ae6d2678e1918ea9cdc3d54a204c6870f26222d835c/fe0364d9b40d597644450555e89c27c90f9a79b946b62502828813073c566414" :answer/id #uuid "bf39fa59-8e27-584b-a24