es. \n\nTherefore, $A$ is diagonalizable, and its Jordan canonical form is\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(4)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The Jordan canonical form is unique up to the order of the Jordan blocks." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110382/ma-source-field/efa32475dad141532738fdfa9d57f405733e37a5748e547c23b9cc1e96957f4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d60456d7-669b-5e35-84bf-81b594b18f3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186162309 :question/answer-fields 17592186159026] {:db/id "q-110384/ma-source-field/515ab47273771789fe8f76527c6af2e6921c7c86bac61ba6f4b39aadacaf9d69/f635b5c316e491002b3806128c13bcb15f68602eb99cf06642fccee93caccc8a" :answer/id #uuid "d0e11af1-776a-5ef9-9c44-f38a0d9993c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110384/ma-source-field/515ab47273771789fe8f76527c6af2e6921c7c86bac61ba6f4b39aadacaf9d69/f50b6b3c8f9dfa99d03096e060c8b90ad81e7798acf9244c4bc04af05a7a7083" :answer/id #uuid "1105886e-0c55-54c4-9e41-0c7b467c09ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110384/ma-source-field/515ab47273771789fe8f76527c6af2e6921c7c86bac61ba6f4b39aadacaf9d69/c66abef76fafb210efd1e3d01727c1b3a379ad1383743367af7a4de24e85739d" :answer/id #uuid "7475dc45-81c3-5570-bfdb-526c21e46e03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110384/ma-source-field/515ab47273771789fe8f76527c6af2e6921c7c86bac61ba6f4b39aadacaf9d69/a922b1c475e7ab2b138f45aae055baf5962322762322211cd306ab29d91defce" 