62bf663bf8328599d47d1b4b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "b2568364-334f-50f4-8bf6-71938e74b4ef"] :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\nLet $Y={X}^{4}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $b$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $0.2$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+d?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y={X}^{4}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $16$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,1,16}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for both $Y=1$ and $Y=16.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.2 \\\\ P(Y=1) & =0.1+0.1 \\\\ P(Y=16) & =0.1+0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=1,b=16,d=0.6,$ and $a+b+d=17.6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111314/ma-source-field/4a415036ebeadf6e53a73969d74fb5923ae201797530ddb9f9cc3529121a272a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/86d50afd5bc338d89158f79b2bfc8a2f3b348dd5452a2551f101483de9a894c7" :answer/id #uuid "1917483a-e41a-50c0-a367-ad84ba924b68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/6568c926dceb08b3c6abc2144c5d05b39c8b2ba116b1e3eb61c40361a7ef95cc" :answer/id #uuid "668fd009-35cb-5151-a226-5758cb5844bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/7104e6b21d3c33ce1458066444960cb4ac3383d6d1f955bd9c663c58ca620881" :answer/id #uuid "1f673251-36a6-5343-9088-515f7b9c6820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/bf0abeb630b74ded1e76fc75b47b8e0a961f01ac06dff504eb3fd6c1c5b76a6b" :answer/id #uuid "f038e0c2-48bd-532f-bbbe-d763ef19f9b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/3af990ea48849b3644a65aa63cbd490ec6ca0e305738b241b767f85f0e8aeaf0" :answer/id #uuid "d0b43087-8938-50cf-8f93-076d97c2600c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211" :answer-field/id #uuid "d189ffbc-6988-5f0d-b648-2094c34edecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/86d50afd5bc338d89158f79b2bfc8a2f3b348dd5452a2551f101483de9a894c7" "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/6568c926dceb08b3c6abc2144c5d05b39c8b2ba116b1e3eb61c40361a7ef95cc" "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/7104e6b21d3c33ce1458066444960cb4ac3383d6d1f955bd9c663c58ca620881" "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/bf0abeb630b74ded1e76fc75b47b8e0a961f01ac06dff504eb3fd6c1c5b76a6b" "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/3af990ea48849b3644a65aa63cbd490ec6ca0e305738b241b767f85f0e8aeaf0"] :answer-field/correct "q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211/bf0abeb630b74ded1e76fc75b47b8e0a961f01ac06dff504eb3fd6c1c5b76a6b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111330" :question/id #uuid "694fef37-1166-5153-b6b0-893dc9dcd03f" :question/math-academy-id "q-111330" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=16-{X}^{2}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.35$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=16-{X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $15$ | $16$ | $15$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,15,16}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for $Y=15.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.35 \\\\ P(Y=15) & =0.15+0.2 \\\\ P(Y=16) & =0.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $15$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.35$ | $0.35$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=15,c=0.35,$ and $a+c=15.35.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111330/ma-source-field/6c6fccdb9781cd580e5b194fc6f2e779e059d3537fcd43fa6004eb9d9fa83211"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f31f7959-b99f-587a-bec3-374e437a2706"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/967651864660b29829144a72415997c2feb607f08a660aa2c