2feb607f08a660aa2cb43c7cc7a22d2dc" "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/89ea3b2ea6272d1de3da917a9b1b16204cb3d34726b3e5f85c233d8f57c2ef24" "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/4e7c0f4162d0aad9c0f95e218e551ee30914d5cc4af2a7623d66ed3970d7a3fd" "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/4bde36a01b3a8e03f8fd76709f5714a5fd2be533c9d4ce890a741b7d36c475ec" "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/da93aac02cda8607f0696f69740079a2088630078f49a62844d16b2c1d3e8371"] :answer-field/correct "q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2/89ea3b2ea6272d1de3da917a9b1b16204cb3d34726b3e5f85c233d8f57c2ef24" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111349" :question/id #uuid "7e63214c-016a-55f5-bcc6-73d6df35ee23" :question/math-academy-id "q-111349" :question/problem "Given that  $\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}$, find a basis for $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\text{Null}(A)$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, a basis for $\\text{Null}(A)$ is\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nsince it is a linearly independent set that generates $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111349/ma-source-field/22e4cfa0cf2fbc374833de7b7abd854358f4446eef1409febeda990dae04bcf2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e66c269-233b-57f8-9dae-46eb78c228bc"] :knowledge-point/questio