5016ffc0399e8cc9d10b882fbb8763b0b8a3a0ddc/2be24b258d1c8100b297597cacf7db0cb6f22f9e2491846693e273412246b9b3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116051" :question/id #uuid "3c40d4d8-93cd-5fd9-9c9b-8b9eaffb8fe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-116051" :question/problem "![](images/30/30b101fa9812c49237ab72c0c4aebd1666df6de80367eb2ee59b33fe0e422d87.png)\n\nIf the diagonals of a square decrease at a rate of $3\\sqrt{2}\\text{ m}\\text{/min}$, at what rate is the perimeter decreasing?" :question/worked-solution "Let $p$ be the perimeter of the square, and $h$ be the length of the diagonal. The relationship between $p$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\np=2\\sqrt{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that each diagonal of the square is decreasing at a rate of $3\\sqrt{2}\\text{ m}\\text{/min},$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=-3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information into the above expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{2})=-12\\text{ m/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the square decreases at $12\\text{ m}/\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-116051/ma-source-field/fb702f1ba880a8130a77c4c5016ffc0399e8cc9d10b882fbb8763b0b8a3a0ddc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1659900c-f6c4-5880-9d2a-4ee68c390432"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/c005a5951a69b9133f8532f721c9305bf985c179de58ccb1771e9bfa020005c3" :answer/id #uuid "759c10d3-8812-51e4-b644-819a5511aa3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "138\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/cdd581fcd75482cbfcfef36f540a0b012b567b72dc110d109d42b2ebae699c32" :answer/id #uuid "b9704ea7-fe23-50df-8ff1-52322eef583e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "186\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/f88bd3092bb3bd1930afda7629c707595f50ccb9541ae6b651e8039f579d8801" :answer/id #uuid "111552bc-03ab-5b73-b002-8c561eed491c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "230\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/1caa6570f4f2c5fcc16791aaddf80edd11b052b3cb1c4cc74b5fbd4a236320c6" :answer/id #uuid "2bf733ca-e8db-54e0-88b3-d8204cd89122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "246\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/c9199d13421dea7cafc198a8340398dc18e1ae427039d4484f0b5c83057716a9" :answer/id #uuid "ea7b0f20-e963-5a14-90b2-fd724d4e32c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "280\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4" :answer-field/id #uuid "928bec64-a4b8-516a-a3c0-19b5dc92551a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/c005a5951a69b9133f8532f721c9305bf985c179de58ccb1771e9bfa020005c3" "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/cdd581fcd75482cbfcfef36f540a0b012b567b72dc110d109d42b2ebae699c32" "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/f88bd3092bb3bd1930afda7629c707595f50ccb9541ae6b651e8039f579d8801" "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/1caa6570f4f2c5fcc16791aaddf80edd11b052b3cb1c4cc74b5fbd4a236320c6" "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/c9199d13421dea7cafc198a8340398dc18e1ae427039d4484f0b5c83057716a9"] :answer-field/correct "q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4/c9199d13421dea7cafc198a8340398dc18e1ae427039d4484f0b5c83057716a9" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116499" :question/id #uuid "d6db5db2-50cf-5e89-b77b-4e40b77e862d" :question/math-academy-id "q-116499" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1a03b31de4f99e5e3ad4a65645beeeb067afc9fdfb0ccb39ada3aff305947f9d.png)\n\nThe length of the rectangular prism shown above is increasing at a rate of $7\\text{ in/min}.$ What is the rate of change of the surface area of the rectangular prism?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, and let $S$ be its surface area. The variables $x$ and $S$ change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =8\\text{ in}, \\\\ z & =12\\text{ in}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\text{ in}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $S$ knowing the rate of change of $x.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nS=2(12)(x)+2x(8)+2(12)(8)=40x+192.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the above expression using $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=7,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(7)=280{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular prism's surface area is increasing at a rate of $280\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116499/ma-source-field/c062300b3df7617d909b89f070cf03c93fab233be41551223f11c8a7d1c78ec4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c29b3f9-5eac-5272-9715-f300211f91ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116499"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/565166cf63c6bd9dbac0d04ca61a0c6f981978aa7e6bc0ef8c867c62d6a1bb9b" :answer/id #uuid "7c656302-c35f-5667-afb2-b247933181dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/61f3f3c6f85611206c2aff87c729df9061c4ff37512598c40317327f624da63a" :answer/id #uuid "721702b3-2d8d-547a-a859-38f4489b077d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/24cc054f51407bd5127f81290b93dc0d4174045b75296455bc29b916953efe66" :answer/id #uuid "d1f9d50c-d199-5878-9d91-1c601ea5f9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/06b1934ddad28062c907dac0d6301b6d874acae263494e4e79b10349b52af175" :answer/id #uuid "1af0f327-7957-509c-92ce-f6ccf0ddb3d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/4ff5c6a42cb789a6a2e859ea420445b0ed532439c8a9bb0fd4d1ca25e6c99279" :answer/id #uuid "e1084c6c-8063-54ae-98d0-49c6dedc72f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbaa4a7f-8da9-5213-ac9e-71081f8e7d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/565166cf63c6bd9dbac0d04ca61a0c6f981978aa7e6bc0ef8c867c62d6a1bb9b" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/61f3f3c6f85611206c2aff87c729df9061c4ff37512598c40317327f624da63a" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/24cc054f51407bd5127f81290b93dc0d4174045b75296455bc29b916953efe66" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/06b1934ddad28062c907dac0d6301b6d874acae263494e4e79b10349b52af175" "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/4ff5c6a42cb789a6a2e859ea420445b0ed532439c8a9bb0fd4d1ca25e6c99279"] :answer-field/correct "q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9/24cc054f51407bd5127f81290b93dc0d4174045b75296455bc29b916953efe66" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116755" :question/id #uuid "9352ab9c-fd90-5378-93d7-0236e8a891cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-116755" :question/problem "![](images/ac/acef9493a9569c023c00e67323f1ffbe8d2f424796205deafb69214838b2c4e2.png)\n\nWater is being poured into a rectangular prism shaped tank. The length and width of this tank are $8\\text{ m}$ and $4\\text{ m},$ respectively. If the height of the water increases at a rate of $0.25\\text{ m/hour}$, determine the rate at which the volume of stored water increases." :question/worked-solution "We define the following variables:\n\n- let $L$ and $W$ be the length and width of the tank, respectively, and\n\n- let $h$ and $V$ be the height and volume of the water in the tank, respectively.\n\nNote that $h$ and $V$ change with time, while $L$ and $W$ are constants. \n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nL=8\\,\\text{m},\\,W=4\\,\\text{m},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{hour}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of the water in the tank:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(8)(4)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =32\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water level is rising at a rate of $8\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116755/ma-source-field/4c11d9556a894c4df3140d3cb2352ae4d6f5c5f0a450b684b732a74f27e6a9b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814ed4fa-33c3-57eb-b843-6268c818fe36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116755"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "05d63814-3721-5df1-9ee4-ce7b9124f4b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "e57920a0-525b-55ec-9484-f65f17f5b566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer/id #uuid "dc1d7c12-42bb-563d-9070-eb5fa55f3bd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "a40c0d41-ab7a-5106-8e75-bfa7c1713fdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer/id #uuid "f4890513-3435-5119-84b3-3f92b4c14b12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a8182c3-02a5-5e68-9327-d52d8bf2cc84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408"] :answer-field/correct "q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117212" :question/id #uuid "0090932a-f451-563b-921a-c105fc8ef9ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-117212" :question/problem "Which of the following values is **not** in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/d2/d2677563c82c37fd1672a806a18524c97ea5ec17cb4f8ef6d8df23b827ba5e81.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The domain of the function is $[-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, the value $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117212/ma-source-field/6b4c5e5d7ba3154f8b45e85b07604e4bed181d754fbcf5cfeee6d5375e406635"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "039f58e5-0f98-58b1-b2f7-9f0ee33ed075"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "95065041-df6a-55e2-ba59-eb39e1ef3c42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4041d9b8-a50e-5114-a489-9911977efeb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "4b365ba9-edc9-5d4f-9d0c-a4e1280cad8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "34eca68d-7384-5ac4-aae3-9fd3ad9100c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "ebf81549-b73c-5aa8-ae6f-2eb529e3d650" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f" :answer-field/id #uuid "b20222d5-4d8b-5ef3-b5e6-cdd257fd9b17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080"] :answer-field/correct "q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117796" :question/id #uuid "5ecbe368-922d-5a9f-956d-5a27886e10df" :question/math-academy-id "q-117796" :question/problem "![](images/92/9278723975d70fec73e313d0e164908ddd339231cb74f75b07c2edce14680111.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-(-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117796/ma-source-field/4ccc4e969c7bbcfdd2ef692af7ee6150487fe939f1839bb2ca4484dfcef80b1f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af228cc4-8be2-5c16-8537-4e5dab4e2ff4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117796"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "c337dc59-1dd1-5197-98b9-3c6fcbf08e62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "dd86b80a-f69a-5bee-9e25-9498124a3b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/82ec26c0001ae04b27cd2a63ab6318b183a710f05feb55d071b767b49c260b88" :answer/id #uuid "a192845d-5444-593f-a294-b8369a05e099" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e570139b-a17c-5e71-8fdc-ac883bda1ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "ae4cbf13-3436-5ca9-a85e-d79666e97f91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b387afd-4a67-578b-8db3-0662089f213d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/82ec26c0001ae04b27cd2a63ab6318b183a710f05feb55d071b767b49c260b88" "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :answer-field/correct "q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c/82ec26c0001ae04b27cd2a63ab6318b183a710f05feb55d071b767b49c260b88" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117799" :question/id #uuid "554b2923-f03c-51dd-9817-6e0a2f8280b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117799" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9ed24a7fa07d6c29e4125c8428fb61a42fc969b99f101c4737bdedf9bf036ff.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}-0=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{3}{4}+(-3)=-\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3x}{4})-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117799/ma-source-field/a847af121f5440ba30de3b6a27de786563945f25670079fb21b1d9737a6b0c1c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9431ea52-88f1-5dea-b8b3-ef48034d0f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9d866037-3d2c-5d4f-87ab-11ddc7a4f74a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c549a040-b264-5669-b784-47b0d206e0bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "743abfee-b36a-5b90-a068-6de3e3d0e361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9cd81f9a-417d-5692-bc82-e493e298ddde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e" :answer-field/id #uuid "63a67a32-debb-51c3-9081-1309e01431cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :answer-field/correct "q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117969" :question/id #uuid "0f77be12-c79a-5d32-a315-5527f2d659be" :question/math-academy-id "q-117969" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x(y-1),\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given $y(1)$ and asked to find $y(4).$ The distance from $x=1$ and $x=4$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(1)=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=1\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=2\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(y-1)=3\\cdot (1-1)=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=3+1=4 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table. \n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(4)≈1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117969/ma-source-field/405e567d94261bb0306af645a87b3114c064889d2841d59407e0359a7232881e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16629348-2577-5c39-8c8c-0f24dbb52c87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117969"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/bb15a40c16849e14349d04337998509e2e5dd918546f76a1e7ff128017e5344d" :answer/id #uuid "76a9807d-df1a-5832-b429-0890d06c222f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5sin⁡(-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/02b21ed2f804e40681c56d757dc3f9c750b444c33d6d36e41df2ee528dd431a1" :answer/id #uuid "bddbf7dd-8781-50a4-b250-66fd8e233371" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{5}sin⁡(-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/ae53b6f2c3582ddd63640d3f6763e2017e3abb6e1a778011c7960c79751074ce" :answer/id #uuid "1866cc81-a61e-52b4-828e-7f095d95514b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-5x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/7caaf868888dca20a3cc9e96f97a6bb9a68503c0024c12e93ca091ec0363e142" :answer/id #uuid "e98140d9-64d1-5b2b-87eb-6cb37aace0e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-\\frac{x}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/2f21e4ef22a71dee952e750116fe1cd7727568cfcc4456ac810b94fe1d8b222f" :answer/id #uuid "7f35edde-ed58-55bc-8274-99043f11903d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-x)-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "0aeaedd6-8135-5962-8437-2a69c460095e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/bb15a40c16849e14349d04337998509e2e5dd918546f76a1e7ff128017e5344d" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/02b21ed2f804e40681c56d757dc3f9c750b444c33d6d36e41df2ee528dd431a1" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/ae53b6f2c3582ddd63640d3f6763e2017e3abb6e1a778011c7960c79751074ce" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/7caaf868888dca20a3cc9e96f97a6bb9a68503c0024c12e93ca091ec0363e142" "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/2f21e4ef22a71dee952e750116fe1cd7727568cfcc4456ac810b94fe1d8b222f"] :answer-field/correct "q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce/bb15a40c16849e14349d04337998509e2e5dd918546f76a1e7ff128017e5344d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118442" :question/id #uuid "e694bf71-afc9-51ff-82ce-ddde47237115" :question/math-academy-id "q-118442" :question/problem "![](images/99/997eb5cc08dcff78cb32f5b47b5d066546854b05f3b066953772e456e713d773.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/1e/1e532c806d81c3c4015d78f814dc4ea3fc3483f22d34ade385894df2e8e7e3c5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=5sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n5sin⁡(-x)=-5sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-5sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-5sin⁡x$ is not among the given options." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118442/ma-source-field/65db2c768a88bd37733794ef1168ec2b2f0dc169537dc01f45122cb2bfea55ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118442"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/4cc5ce2bf51ef2cea963a2b0e9fba8bdde47c67b0e1ebb376fa2426d7a5b320d" :answer/id #uuid "62375a92-edd9-5873-9edf-ef0ddd9dccaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6sin⁡(-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/ceb864b32489eb05b775234e217b03de849bb4a78fcb3aa8316870e9c793f581" :answer/id #uuid "fbef0156-6d81-5b0b-80b2-e4c086df567d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{6}sin⁡(-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/f0a6cdbe485a0a166dcc253e40acce3464ba86be04fe95c7e27d50f436718931" :answer/id #uuid "ab0aa795-c7d5-534e-922f-0ead75cd6cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-6x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/8ce4c07316f3d30ed17f2fe0870e5a5a5546a5dc17be54a95e79ee0282aa05a8" :answer/id #uuid "839a4786-7b8b-587f-884b-34a3e1fb530a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-\\frac{x}{6})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/62c1e8866421ff11d8cbc2007161c2108d986214057fcd3c1fd158a62656fba1" :answer/id #uuid "1f1a872d-3b88-5a7f-8b75-ab249c2d63b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-x)+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0f56dd-8c86-5cbb-8889-d10079bd9452" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/4cc5ce2bf51ef2cea963a2b0e9fba8bdde47c67b0e1ebb376fa2426d7a5b320d" "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/ceb864b32489eb05b775234e217b03de849bb4a78fcb3aa8316870e9c793f581" "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/f0a6cdbe485a0a166dcc253e40acce3464ba86be04fe95c7e27d50f436718931" "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/8ce4c07316f3d30ed17f2fe0870e5a5a5546a5dc17be54a95e79ee0282aa05a8" "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/62c1e8866421ff11d8cbc2007161c2108d986214057fcd3c1fd158a62656fba1"] :answer-field/correct "q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067/4cc5ce2bf51ef2cea963a2b0e9fba8bdde47c67b0e1ebb376fa2426d7a5b320d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118443" :question/id #uuid "ef71e5dd-2133-5139-bcc4-313a9e867ac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-118443" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f012ee5880b4ec6c4c2cad4aa44da672b789f21c7f9969dcec50a25596e47c4b.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/bc/bc61bf27fb210e0dc849829d5c287936fcb3f73bc279e98af8a64ba4085b8309.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=6sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n6sin⁡(-x)=-6sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-6sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-6sin⁡x$ is not among the given options." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118443/ma-source-field/fa57a45512a84005293dedad0287b6a60fccbf25fd4ea7ff371f6b0d9eaa8067"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118443"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/4af9e753006c21c2d14e93a270d27ae907496bc7f51d967c50fdb35b5ead3aa8" :answer/id #uuid "6cfc929f-0e67-5e47-80b6-d2949d1be4b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/7c60f3b3780b304d71d9fe80faecb3c11a90e99f83c54d400650dfee40c61c34" :answer/id #uuid "395e4984-cf1d-534b-b01f-09b03aa00ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/b60f9fbb79fe16ddaa756f6164a78ba5a068817c4341b0904850daf993954539" :answer/id #uuid "796c5808-234b-5385-a5e5-513d3b55563c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/6b5237a365ad617c078fc4a8a1e0352898cc351c14ad6cb479f29591b39d08cd" :answer/id #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/10aa8de7a21d1b49fe76a72df1ff0a44b76e42dd3395fa9f4827723c1e5ea9de" :answer/id #uuid "2339eddd-c520-53fc-835c-406bf5642b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7d8f65-a93b-5daa-b8fa-34a0b4f4a5ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/4af9e753006c21c2d14e93a270d27ae907496bc7f51d967c50fdb35b5ead3aa8" "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/7c60f3b3780b304d71d9fe80faecb3c11a90e99f83c54d400650dfee40c61c34" "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/b60f9fbb79fe16ddaa756f6164a78ba5a068817c4341b0904850daf993954539" "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/6b5237a365ad617c078fc4a8a1e0352898cc351c14ad6cb479f29591b39d08cd" "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/10aa8de7a21d1b49fe76a72df1ff0a44b76e42dd3395fa9f4827723c1e5ea9de"] :answer-field/correct "q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515/6b5237a365ad617c078fc4a8a1e0352898cc351c14ad6cb479f29591b39d08cd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119039" :question/id #uuid "9f503fbb-9abb-5178-8aa2-5b5187c150ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-119039" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=20{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =20\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+C \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119039/ma-source-field/34b30c9aa17c407c316a8f36144f5a2e07d9ad2e7548ec1a13ec9aac4324a515"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/286ba69cf41c0487e20cb3d4ea67f6b65bb53e73662ff2f39923d42171dee80b" :answer/id #uuid "dbad500b-d968-57c7-8690-6808ade1af6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" :answer/id #uuid "5f5d956d-a3db-5f17-a60a-c65874e02299" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "602aa483-d67f-5404-8467-f27f01940f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" :answer/id #uuid "14d09f20-c9c1-5eab-bc98-c123faf3e1b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=4\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :answer/id #uuid "427f7f46-348f-5d5b-8214-11acace487f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=6\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2" :answer-field/id #uuid "695e7fd0-433d-51f0-b01d-00b9f5bc61a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/286ba69cf41c0487e20cb3d4ea67f6b65bb53e73662ff2f39923d42171dee80b" "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/d5def0cf746ec332768f9da3bbd3918000db01e741698aca0cf711527ac7cb72" "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/0ef8964ec0a97853c9de78640006c9267484858b6037a9251f0953a6b60d7cbd" "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/1417faeeecb9abcec842b42bc312e82d299a8ac8f43684f3e20cdc301cbc99c4" "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da"] :answer-field/correct "q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2/8a8e4d981f70dfe4d9a30d5693836556ef8e6ad73d426cc0e557d2e2924ec9da" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120844" :question/id #uuid "0588ded7-d4bd-5616-b35b-33100943aa76" :question/math-academy-id "q-120844" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=4\\,\\text{s},$  determine the moment in time when the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "The particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$\n\nFirst, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(4)=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{4}{(4)}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =1+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{t}-\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nNow, we find the moments in time when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{t}-\\frac{2}{3} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{t} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ t & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary when $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120844/ma-source-field/6748fe4b65fa5ab2646b8a810410f3ce54f8b222ae383e29482866450d5f9fd2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c28b400d-9ec3-53c6-8e33-0133598ed143"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120844"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d99dcb4d-2a83-549a-b986-4a60429f6baa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/25d79eef8a16f080073a8e877263e916b245aa7f9e3282b422f7b7d7005baf31" :answer/id #uuid "197ae8e0-022c-5701-9bc2-270d31cca02d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "631461f4-e54f-5325-b27b-475e158a4548" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "98436ba7-22e8-5883-92bc-f2a392e4c571" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "111eb72f-77db-56c0-809e-6b4a599df81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685" :answer-field/id #uuid "34d0bc62-23d7-51e0-a40e-82b353c65411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/25d79eef8a16f080073a8e877263e916b245aa7f9e3282b422f7b7d7005baf31" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e"] :answer-field/correct "q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685/25d79eef8a16f080073a8e877263e916b245aa7f9e3282b422f7b7d7005baf31" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120911" :question/id #uuid "13b68e5e-22d6-5fa0-a4a4-6c5d1f4c0a70" :question/math-academy-id "q-120911" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(3).$ The distance from $x=0$ and $x=3$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(0)=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=1\\cdot \\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot 1=1 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+1=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ |\n| $3$ | $2+2\\sqrt{2}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈2+2\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120911/ma-source-field/74da69d2eed49bb4b3dbbe78c484b78c1ba5b655a7a744c54603e77024f22685"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16629348-2577-5c39-8c8c-0f24dbb52c87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "f31a39b5-ddea-5435-ad94-3285f142b3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7" :answer/id #uuid "7062ec22-777c-5ee0-8265-a643d026997a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/5af4b542c90e395f5f4af499da66123a12579005cf0807c6a5587df7b0db3f99" :answer/id #uuid "d779dff4-110a-560a-8225-d7034da334e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer/id #uuid "4c9e9422-5b2e-544f-8018-890315cb6fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15" :answer/id #uuid "2e82f7e5-3527-59eb-986a-5f3b990235ed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The particle is never stationary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510" :answer-field/id #uuid "379f8f68-62eb-5f9b-956e-558338f11c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/68b9609c73019519096d74c9eb72d7cf21e3a1157aa880ff36e5de58ba989cf7" "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/5af4b542c90e395f5f4af499da66123a12579005cf0807c6a5587df7b0db3f99" "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/95bc528a42f83cd4a53eb9e36d6b727f32c1b0eb864272fd8716dcc591ea8d15"] :answer-field/correct "q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121736" :question/id #uuid "942f342e-d375-5134-864c-b37213f6cf64" :question/math-academy-id "q-121736" :question/problem "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-4t+8),{t}^{4}-\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-4t+8),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-\\frac{8}{3}{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t-4}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=2, \\\\ 4{t}^{2}(t-2)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=2$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-121736/ma-source-field/04ed02c86c6d36dcefbe97db953485b1f2e887986e68a767c50d45fb82245510"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11a24997-1f1e-5968-a331-980ca14be2f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/5d2f716a33503eec53ec624986c4300a233a9102d878bf79ff6824e1dcb44066" :answer/id #uuid "a43b3ff9-d167-5f2a-a49d-342a3fc83921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/3dd270d6a60d3cca5c51453976550b43d34a8f4b795339dccc464246d105afd4" :answer/id #uuid "676387be-6610-5f16-9796-2babd5ce0f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-5t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/3491646a42db77289598d95b8f5c16a651a6d6b27de88c98f905b14f386cad9c" :answer/id #uuid "2ca1dcb5-771f-59eb-81e9-1e595c34e462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/082e0caab51ce208ae0528816a06183fc96974475d89be556b05c471a11680f2" :answer/id #uuid "1875e854-1900-58b4-bea8-ec0e5d6629b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-9t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/4288615a2a9057157b162694e159812cbe1a4c4b2d93c2dfaf9761159997a3ce" :answer/id #uuid "ddbb623b-497e-5583-a206-85cecb99534f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d025741-a121-5bf5-a673-350aefe4b1cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/5d2f716a33503eec53ec624986c4300a233a9102d878bf79ff6824e1dcb44066" "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/3dd270d6a60d3cca5c51453976550b43d34a8f4b795339dccc464246d105afd4" "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/3491646a42db77289598d95b8f5c16a651a6d6b27de88c98f905b14f386cad9c" "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/082e0caab51ce208ae0528816a06183fc96974475d89be556b05c471a11680f2" "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/4288615a2a9057157b162694e159812cbe1a4c4b2d93c2dfaf9761159997a3ce"] :answer-field/correct "q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d/082e0caab51ce208ae0528816a06183fc96974475d89be556b05c471a11680f2" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122527" :question/id #uuid "757cf839-4729-500e-9a5f-1ad15eb1165b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122527" :question/problem "Consider the line integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}(2x-3y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the segment of the line $\\frac{x}{2}=1-\\frac{3y}{2}$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(-4,2).$ Which of the following is the missing expression under the integral on the right?\n\n*Hint: Use the parameter $y=t.$*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the given curve can be expressed in the form $x=x(y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=1-\\frac{3y}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2-3y\n$$\n\nTherefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2-3t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2-3t,\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $0\\le t\\le 2$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =-3\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2x-3y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(2-3t)-3t \\\\  & =4-9t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(2x-3y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-9t)\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-9t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122527/ma-source-field/8ee3a790b240a7a1d6fd4901de84bd4b3fd2871ec628e261715d507009fb842d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b638f71-529a-5a6f-a68e-805f11080587"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/0825dcb7a69ebabd5bb74e00d5edddbbd0b41b66432679e41fe9631f6ee66ad6" :answer/id #uuid "a308d91e-d998-5724-b79b-60e732336f24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x<{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/401c3c4316729c507b622c5a9b2a55417262449150fc2ff6a25ec2a7eb04d608" :answer/id #uuid "c7ad4611-2a25-5515-9a96-aa614194aed2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/fba306cd078c2281b6de4fb6b4c1064ce0681091bc4e2dd63e5f83b8422493a5" :answer/id #uuid "689f2980-5408-56a2-a1df-2b0d8b222552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2},\\,x>1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/455fc28822738f730b71dc47f30bb2d6ffc6c168b01f2a7dfd73a9b23efc0eb8" :answer/id #uuid "185f7409-0599-54ba-a0cd-ab79287fc960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2},\\,x\\ne 1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/e26c548e81959f6718d306c77b83baf2dad0c9ba4a863f0d37f854f5c1d9e807" :answer/id #uuid "c6f293d2-0d9e-5145-8206-ea5780ccb464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "48ae7e1a-6a16-5754-8819-ca18faede750" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/0825dcb7a69ebabd5bb74e00d5edddbbd0b41b66432679e41fe9631f6ee66ad6" "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/401c3c4316729c507b622c5a9b2a55417262449150fc2ff6a25ec2a7eb04d608" "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/fba306cd078c2281b6de4fb6b4c1064ce0681091bc4e2dd63e5f83b8422493a5" "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/455fc28822738f730b71dc47f30bb2d6ffc6c168b01f2a7dfd73a9b23efc0eb8" "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/e26c548e81959f6718d306c77b83baf2dad0c9ba4a863f0d37f854f5c1d9e807"] :answer-field/correct "q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5/e26c548e81959f6718d306c77b83baf2dad0c9ba4a863f0d37f854f5c1d9e807" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122663" :question/id #uuid "f9d1b0c7-3a1c-573d-9729-ab5857b0ca01" :question/math-academy-id "q-122663" :question/problem "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{1/x}\\,j\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),\\,Q(x,y)=({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{1/x}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the logarithm is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\nx-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,x>{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator of the exponent vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122663/ma-source-field/5eaa799e5e411deb6a82b12e3a79e7e2e3fe97e0ad678fe661272c4ab40f3aa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67b7ea90-38e0-54b5-b76e-816beb0d48f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122663"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/cbef05226c7d15e8b844ae10934b5689df811893fbaf4f620db7c6e93145d3e0" :answer/id #uuid "a45de57b-7567-5153-b536-079a7493dfff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/46e89f817a5e619d7cfb26cb98e77ebeb64af70d0ca4e8b5aa3a5cc1bd212513" :answer/id #uuid "f3e7a6e3-452b-57d7-bee7-a456f2cb7f08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/364bb9b83d166f6ff99b68e36f5c461d4d526ac7afc6f83ac74911a7287ea911" :answer/id #uuid "173b53e6-f27b-52cd-8b04-8ca55a358b44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/1a60e5de710e5c160808a7009d5e0fa133d5a44d26e20970a7bd66d0bd0c6565" :answer/id #uuid "d5deb70e-b37a-53c8-afc0-f67c23624ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{5t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/83c337c9e2e9a5e5dc57c764aff6c9ccef4bafb6f732a2225d16a48eb962774d" :answer/id #uuid "84a43112-1761-5fc6-adc6-94c0086bfedf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}+5,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f3589e3-9365-51aa-8bbb-05d8e6a481a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/cbef05226c7d15e8b844ae10934b5689df811893fbaf4f620db7c6e93145d3e0" "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/46e89f817a5e619d7cfb26cb98e77ebeb64af70d0ca4e8b5aa3a5cc1bd212513" "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/364bb9b83d166f6ff99b68e36f5c461d4d526ac7afc6f83ac74911a7287ea911" "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/1a60e5de710e5c160808a7009d5e0fa133d5a44d26e20970a7bd66d0bd0c6565" "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/83c337c9e2e9a5e5dc57c764aff6c9ccef4bafb6f732a2225d16a48eb962774d"] :answer-field/correct "q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66/cbef05226c7d15e8b844ae10934b5689df811893fbaf4f620db7c6e93145d3e0" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123292" :question/id #uuid "811bbc59-9fc3-5b4b-bd9e-2e09752150a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123292" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩$, then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int ({e}^{2t}+5)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123292/ma-source-field/c270f1b3a42d76855142494dee0eca2f418589f51ec3a49c540b40b176814b66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123294/ma-source-field/b8b0d70eb2acd759c5514d0292e01ba6adca19be80ce0fbc610df4735e5b4386/d156d9b33137630a9eda1bf3baaedf83f93e5f78b5257896584ed7bbb53d240f" :answer/id #uuid "773252d0-6e9f-5e6f-ad08-105990cdd9e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{4}+2,\\,\\frac{t}{8}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123294/ma-source-field/b8b0d70eb2acd759c5514d0292e01ba6adca19be80ce0fbc610df4735e5b4386/42a1b7ba9a8ea656c8eddd797ccf2c3c7f42a41f0b9fc86b5abc83f910a4a7bc" :answer/id #uuid "b6a9a238-62ac-5621-ae23-bfa91834e092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨t+4,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123294/ma-source-field/b8b0d70eb2acd759c5514d0292e01ba6adca19be80ce0fbc610df4735e5b4386/214dc32590a6a2bacc60b97cd5975c361d4eab33adb8b1d5657dfea0d70bad7a" :answer/id #uuid "c9e81bae-2705-548d-95b6-765f54a06b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2}-4t,\\,\\frac{t}{8}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123294/ma-source-field/b8b0d70eb2acd759c5514d0292e01ba6adca19be80ce0fbc610df4735e5b4386/d64b0b3f937be67868a730c2ca058fb3faa2e13c2ca8d