eee4bb13b5cb96d6b9ca11f7984674a5f382f39eda575542e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126353" :question/id #uuid "7c5c71ff-a77d-5a86-8573-305cd57f3d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126353" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126353/ma-source-field/da8cdce12518ae4af2bdab866d3effffd7f73e788be47df4fef6ed34215c96b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127003/ma-source-field/e1ce45116c2f64902a2dd0e180450afeba3efbf3588d38ebcae4a4796213ad1f/ad7f241f53510a9ca0600dbdca258328e851b2e62dec9574f1c76c7377a985f4" :answer/id #uuid "2f8093a4-96c1-598c-86b0-87a9d0382d52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127003/ma-source-field/e1ce45116c2f64902a2dd0e180450afeba3efbf3588d38ebcae4a4796213ad1f/715a5dc01e26422d8510a1beb24fdc9712b04b8aff4b0962afbeea86cb2ff847" :answer/id #uuid "59b98ec9-bd61-5aaf-ab04-a002f394a95c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127003/ma-source