difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127033/ma-source-field/bfcc0e096b781e2436a7e4b575c2ad5d7c02cb07f5bb4b0daa853d70ff6277cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127033"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/be3259896afa1423c28cb048f63048895fc32fc9364453a587d76de108a1ce4f" :answer/id #uuid "5860855f-9a3e-5177-8f82-b305b25602d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/84e0bc49d89bd54579e3e6c5fe6b3075f7dee03b50529c36f4d6c6b67c61bf39" :answer/id #uuid "084dd163-8456-51dc-abdd-4a5eea95cc92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/a1a67ffd49b4387905f866a086810e8db8bd6525de0a7b389623404f9668ad74" :answer/id #uuid "8f677f3f-e28b-556f-866e-a1bb72653998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/a69445603195bf752badf828a3f6151c424684133bbff61549083303438ddf73" :answer/id #uuid "4327286d-a7cb-5d9d-8513-bee55df9202d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/8bae5eec068df3a053d7e6232c229408b45dd7c61e43679a444241829c59f4ea" :answer/id #uuid "a2a7ad62-1f98-5677-b05c-070f0505e36c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e390087c-f3c4-5e5d-895a-6dad0ea160b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/be3259896afa1423c28cb048f63048895fc32fc9364453a587d76de108a1ce4f" "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/84e0bc49d89bd54579e3e6c5fe6b3075f7dee03b50529c36f4d6c6b67c61bf39" "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/a1a67ffd49b4387905f866a086810e8db8bd6525de0a7b389623404f9668ad74" "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/a69445603195bf752badf828a3f6151c424684133bbff61549083303438ddf73" "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/8bae5eec068df3a053d7e6232c229408b45dd7c61e43679a444241829c59f4ea"] :answer-field/correct "q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b/a1a67ffd49b4387905f866a086810e8db8bd6525de0a7b389623404f9668ad74" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127333" :question/id #uuid "d9ec2fe9-559e-547b-851b-6351eb71769b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127333" :question/problem "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}⟨1,\\,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}⟨1,\\,2t⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}})⟨1,\\,2t⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{4t}{(4{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}⟨1,\\,2t⟩+\\frac{1}{(4{t}^{2}+1)^{1/2}}⟨0,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(4{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}[-4t⟨1,\\,2t⟩+(4{t}^{2}+1)⟨0,\\,2⟩] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(4{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}⟨-4t,\\,2\\,⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{(4(1)^{2}+1)^{3/2}}⟨-4(1),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{5}^{3}}}⟨-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}‖⟨-2,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the principal normal vector to the curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1⟩}{(\\frac{2}{5})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $N$ and $T$ at the point where $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1)\\cdot T(1) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1⟩\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨1,\\,2⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(⟨-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,2⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((-2)(1)+(1)(2)) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127333/ma-source-field/e27806062ebfbfa7dfd426fadfd231af3b24f840289f37878a2290a9b832a10b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "930466fc-c7fe-51a5-8634-818abddd0da9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/4c88caadd52e2d8f4829176aeb81fbc02f56e6447d4300724efd586af13332c5" :answer/id #uuid "7a9faa04-0ff3-58c0-9180-ad10d99b2911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/4a2b0acb7d11a10262d00202be782976f53c13052d33cd298a59517d6d0310f1" :answer/id #uuid "60fb6e8c-68a1-5734-b535-b2fcb695213a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/be3259896afa1423c28cb048f63048895fc32fc9364453a587d76de108a1ce4f" :answer/id #uuid "5e0ef47a-49f6-5f7c-85d7-c6f8163f2fcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/1f474891f4a1f048839f0a9262ee683892518d77135db05c550db0439728cd3a" :answer/id #uuid "cb3a5249-e2a5-57f9-8e7b-da061704300d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/f0a412b7b5663925a4bae2889dfd8d87cfbcc013351d4b3e8cd52ee2184f2ca0" :answer/id #uuid "caeb96ab-86e7-5128-afdc-6b279a672893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\sqrt{2},1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55" :answer-field/id #uuid "e61eec78-2599-57fe-a41d-57c6c6d95dc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/4c88caadd52e2d8f4829176aeb81fbc02f56e6447d4300724efd586af13332c5" "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/4a2b0acb7d11a10262d00202be782976f53c13052d33cd298a59517d6d0310f1" "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/be3259896afa1423c28cb048f63048895fc32fc9364453a587d76de108a1ce4f" "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/1f474891f4a1f048839f0a9262ee683892518d77135db05c550db0439728cd3a" "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/f0a412b7b5663925a4bae2889dfd8d87cfbcc013351d4b3e8cd52ee2184f2ca0"] :answer-field/correct "q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55/4a2b0acb7d11a10262d00202be782976f53c13052d33cd298a59517d6d0310f1" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127583" :question/id #uuid "d020d9fa-ec2e-5a71-a105-bba07f29c4ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-127583" :question/problem "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(0)=⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,{q}^{′}(0)=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{4+t})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+t)}^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{2}{4+t}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2}{{(4+0)}^{2}}\\cdot q(0)+\\frac{2}{4+0}\\cdot {q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(-⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩+4⟨1,0⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{8}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{8}⟨3,-\\sqrt{3}⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\cdot N(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(0)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127583/ma-source-field/cf839011e3a3489293070c7f55004ba2aec7e75938f9b1ca447f7b3583bf0f55"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe665f-05e8-5183-9c98-cb760af0ae02"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/34753b22b76591c1ca7269c8ce358838ff4b9da2ca798e04380229d8c49794e0" :answer/id #uuid "6f58a28b-8a69-51ea-9356-d11140bffa6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/b2f0965dae5c3b3856d9338e44e5e5404d1285ed1bf70896b860082cefe46f54" :answer/id #uuid "94b7fac8-b0d0-5073-bd6a-e851bd44f67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-1,-\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/bd4c08f0cab0cc77a4a4009435431f58da5787c715a0137c985e6469e36d6873" :answer/id #uuid "25f226b0-16a9-5f5d-aa1f-dd6c1a36838c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/d5e55947c3e746c10730d4def9a1743c912e7db6c0bff67d1c14fca37d389c3a" :answer/id #uuid "a1f5b218-1e89-5311-a291-97235fe4d002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-\\sqrt{2},1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/fc736c88f73a4907600b6a849093e7520900e0ca6911d2556e96fe961f18d43a" :answer/id #uuid "413846d8-f5f3-5bd5-b545-4953038ddd12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,0,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d103e9f6-a851-56bd-8b50-38d9ebf224a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/34753b22b76591c1ca7269c8ce358838ff4b9da2ca798e04380229d8c49794e0" "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/b2f0965dae5c3b3856d9338e44e5e5404d1285ed1bf70896b860082cefe46f54" "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/bd4c08f0cab0cc77a4a4009435431f58da5787c715a0137c985e6469e36d6873" "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/d5e55947c3e746c10730d4def9a1743c912e7db6c0bff67d1c14fca37d389c3a" "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/fc736c88f73a4907600b6a849093e7520900e0ca6911d2556e96fe961f18d43a"] :answer-field/correct "q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c/bd4c08f0cab0cc77a4a4009435431f58da5787c715a0137c985e6469e36d6873" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127598" :question/id #uuid "811d16c6-f719-59c2-bae0-963973f1dd90" :question/math-academy-id "q-127598" :question/problem "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}+1}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(0)=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},1⟩,\\,{q}^{′}(0)=⟨1,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}+1}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}+1})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{({e}^{t}+1)^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}+1}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{({e}^{0}+1)^{2}}\\cdot q(0)+\\frac{1}{{e}^{0}+1}\\cdot {q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}q(0)+\\frac{1}{2}{q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}⟨1,\\sqrt{2},1⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(-⟨1,\\sqrt{2},1⟩+2⟨1,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},0⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}⟨1,0,-1⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\cdot N(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(0)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{2},1⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(1(1)+\\sqrt{2}(0)+1(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(1+0-1) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127598/ma-source-field/36ffad73cd4b037904f85cabe4f213d5380d031b2bc72de119e59d881fe7b39c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe665f-05e8-5183-9c98-cb760af0ae02"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/23d6eb10ea16b2fe9c2e857ef5c0e51f1310635779296a0b62b08af7515d1069" :answer/id #uuid "c61b2cbe-e283-5d14-b24c-72dded057638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(-\\sqrt{2}\\,i+\\,j+k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/cc13829a4e396f8ad37124356207300cad8a0d3cd307ae851e14a95ca535ff7b" :answer/id #uuid "6f1c6878-8ab0-51e2-8005-62b32908bc7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/52c1612c9a22627d023af4081b2292c327043326879aed302432edb380052e0f" :answer/id #uuid "843c6fdf-9f38-56ac-8525-881bcff219b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i-\\,j+2\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/86cf2a9cef2c8df0e50ad3c2c643aa72ffdc8a0678b6b6ca0feee2ea9e4ee42e" :answer/id #uuid "d5b83354-a308-50ea-9ee4-85aaf20726b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-j+k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/f7530a2abefc24722c990cca004da5d8b292e4e3760bd097c1525ffa018dc049" :answer/id #uuid "1f7cd7b0-03c7-513f-a03d-32eb59e6232b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(\\sqrt{2}\\,i-2\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714" :answer-field/id #uuid "07a28c00-4228-59a1-bd55-b03951c2d0fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/23d6eb10ea16b2fe9c2e857ef5c0e51f1310635779296a0b62b08af7515d1069" "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/cc13829a4e396f8ad37124356207300cad8a0d3cd307ae851e14a95ca535ff7b" "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/52c1612c9a22627d023af4081b2292c327043326879aed302432edb380052e0f" "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/86cf2a9cef2c8df0e50ad3c2c643aa72ffdc8a0678b6b6ca0feee2ea9e4ee42e" "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/f7530a2abefc24722c990cca004da5d8b292e4e3760bd097c1525ffa018dc049"] :answer-field/correct "q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714/86cf2a9cef2c8df0e50ad3c2c643aa72ffdc8a0678b6b6ca0feee2ea9e4ee42e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127600" :question/id #uuid "0d57e43b-681d-5aa1-a53c-acdd85847d41" :question/math-academy-id "q-127600" :question/problem "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=0$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(0)=\\sqrt{2}\\,i+j+k,\\,{q}^{′}(0)=-2\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{2(0)}{({0}^{2}+2)^{2}}\\cdot q(0)+\\frac{1}{{0}^{2}+2}\\cdot {q}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =0(\\sqrt{2}\\,i+j+k)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =-j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(0)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{-j+k}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-j+k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\cdot N(0) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(0)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-j+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}\\,i+j+k)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-j+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(-j\\cdot j+k\\cdot k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(-1+1) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127600/ma-source-field/b9c1f50c89d7454061a14d36e4fb0a534c87f35529cd6a49efd90d9420ad0714"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe665f-05e8-5183-9c98-cb760af0ae02"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/0a39b98f8bc8c43c345a4bae7e8d899031d3abc4e6d432eb59023f3e4a934d9e" :answer/id #uuid "bce01ee3-e62d-5dbf-8ab7-ab7ffd839257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/3c21bc415faa3a987801a2012718d7249c83fd2bae5109c3b81e2c6c1a675230" :answer/id #uuid "cb1c7834-02fe-5c78-b2fe-aa883eb34976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/405b6d8e1398e68dbb5d7724d547e08f62dccb2ce3cbc21fce36ec120b6725de" :answer/id #uuid "c2e1ebaa-2f3e-5015-b022-3d3df282249e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/81048e996037ec00ebd726d167ee0e4dea99dbed7e0902b4c74051f50a81a729" :answer/id #uuid "717243f7-02ac-50c5-9655-63bba2b18b42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/f124288bd3d21f14877ebfd267ce89e7d4073e646afae54376bf8b1ce2836291" :answer/id #uuid "fcfc218d-9756-5117-a5b1-a400cbe24097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a" :answer-field/id #uuid "16d27f97-4329-5b65-b357-06a7d75d56ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/0a39b98f8bc8c43c345a4bae7e8d899031d3abc4e6d432eb59023f3e4a934d9e" "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/3c21bc415faa3a987801a2012718d7249c83fd2bae5109c3b81e2c6c1a675230" "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/405b6d8e1398e68dbb5d7724d547e08f62dccb2ce3cbc21fce36ec120b6725de" "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/81048e996037ec00ebd726d167ee0e4dea99dbed7e0902b4c74051f50a81a729" "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/f124288bd3d21f14877ebfd267ce89e7d4073e646afae54376bf8b1ce2836291"] :answer-field/correct "q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a/f124288bd3d21f14877ebfd267ce89e7d4073e646afae54376bf8b1ce2836291" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736" :question/id #uuid "9fd0e8ab-5ed1-5462-b099-07b3173547c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127736" :question/problem "Calculate ${Z}^{-1}$ where\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Z$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=1\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 2=2\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z{Z}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Z}^{-1}Z & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127736/ma-source-field/4f4b954a0650e5a02557ff8c2a2e2e61e6cf4b79fed21bd4bd21e47488d1269a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127737/ma-source-field/4b455212074f8a6318f8f9676766203401985ad4af4d22496ec12e4706af70e9/3c9f82e9df6d3eafc7e4e9877bd217eeeaacd9f8fe6cde854c1f75645