To determine the number of absences there were in a class whose size is $20$ students, we locate $20$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(20,6).$ Therefore, there was a total of $6$ absences in the month for the class with $20$ students." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134085/ma-source-field/410c04f8b1c31fe53eb0a8a4b90b1cfbb7f3980a241fb3afeb3edbba3bb3682f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f99f2aa-f977-5d6e-ae62-a826a897ba9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134085"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/070f2b56dbe050630c4363adfc797fc58ea7428b344d273f031beabe7cd00a74" :answer/id #uuid "6c5bb798-cec3-5a92-9d75-11208ba367e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "61.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/567a64af3d04fe8efb60cb1e6ffdee37abc4f4e013e17830ec47d7c2bd0134fe" :answer/id #uuid "577131db-9008-56b9-a467-51c63bcf9b9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "67\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/a760d88544f9e6d6751fa895a91d61a1a3c62de45b6b6481bdacaad4229d6c1e" :answer/id #uuid "ea7e78d9-3274-5840-9bbb-71ef4bb5921d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70.6\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/9100b1dbbb946d559fdc454853210252487344d1dcbac664210d0980ddad3817" :answer/id #uuid "af98f4ef-a70e-5c69-9cbd-4bc71919c6e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75.1\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/17fd5cccc0c009af443b9a90a37e700541651671791b5545778d8ce8f5399d75" :answer/id #uuid "4d938cd5-a02b-597a-b438-1708be6fb7f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80.2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a5589d-c173-52b7-aa4e-ec8dcdd731a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/070f2b56dbe050630c4363adfc797fc58ea7428b344d273f031beabe7cd00a74" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/567a64af3d04fe8efb60cb1e6ffdee37abc4f4e013e17830ec47d7c2bd0134fe" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/a760d88544f9e6d6751fa895a91d61a1a3c62de45b6b6481bdacaad4229d6c1e" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/9100b1dbbb946d559fdc454853210252487344d1dcbac664210d0980ddad3817" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/17fd5cccc0c009af443b9a90a37e700541651671791b5545778d8ce8f5399d75"] :answer-field/correct "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/a760d88544f9e6d6751fa895a91d61a1a3c62de45b6b6481bdacaad4229d6c1e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135105" :question/id #uuid "04947b95-8a1f-567f-948f-2de5de86130e" :question/math-academy-id "q-135105" :question/problem "An object is projected vertically down from a height of $0.6\\,\\text{km}$ and hits the ground in $6\\,\\text{s}.$ What was the initial velocity of the object?\n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The object falls for $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- We can find the distance the object falls in meters as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =0.6\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\text{km}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\cancel{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}} \\\\  & =0.6\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =600\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (600) & =u(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(6)^{2} \\\\ 600 & =6u+176.4 \\\\ 423.6 & =6u \\\\ u & =70.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the object was $u=70.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c3fb8a8-343a-5046-afce-83db17ec1039"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-136311/ma-source-field/3322ad499f30df09b5186f6fc3f02a17c5cacd56f7a828a15f2ed1cda9ddfcd2/345c11f7f98171853efa370fe20967fb1c9589dfd947e3929f7a221ee89abd95" :answer/id #uuid "7a65e5ff-4a0a-57d3-b7ca-a7d4f13983ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.65\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136311/ma-source-field/3322ad499f30df09b5186f6fc3f02a17c5cacd56f7a828a15f2ed1cda9ddfcd2/1ac0e6b5de832e5ee3bef9799bcbb22caf619d3c5248eb43bcdd023885971ed9" :answer/id #uuid "d1defb76-8459-59c2-b2f3-882cb4