},\\,y(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{4} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141113/ma-source-field/f4b14c6b2ca55491a1fc127585c041467e8dc29fe66c015f768a8c992a0c619a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141115/ma-source-field/6d307acd0451d69023785b1d04885f5f25a27061517acbdb414c97b1942b66ef/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "408ad86d-b3e2-50fe-ba49-d6d10e8b89e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141115/ma-source-field/6d307acd0451d69023785b1d04885f5f25a27061517acbdb414c97b1942b66ef/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b092bcb2-de91-5a2a-9a1c-b1cf1cdf0b26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141115/ma-source-field/6d307acd0451d69023785b1d04885f5f25a27061517acbdb414c97b1942b66ef/72443840a1994ef4e387277621cd8f464de0132f9c0b12ec6eac8b3cee6eca7d" :answer/id #uuid "d1591666-636c-5480-9f22-08f9eeec3613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141115/ma-source-field/6d307acd0451d69023785b1d04885f5f