a-105e-56e5-bee4-742b27b9d838" :question/math-academy-id "q-141999" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8b237f9e857b1ed87de447aa79c14d359429e71d8afe7ab8eab201eba7ffb6af.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is  $B+2D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}=2.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Therefore, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+2D=2+2\\cdot (1)=2+2=4.$  \n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141999/ma-source-field/d1e4091c5e8ad6c936e75fc933962122d1b54f60f1d5b52ce64100a5cbab417a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "251fc1e5-eecc-5524-8fcc-50a9a87bac4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d1a7f65b-0eec-54b0-bd1b-1489777d7346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "1477d75c-69cc-56f6-83aa-951c0dfbc5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c3a9476a-83e1-5900-adda-60bacbc12a44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "823522a9-4039-541d-b6e1-6b18113ea496" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408" :answer-field/id #uuid "25043d55-6e38-5a47-9ce8-35564e623dc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :answer-field/correct "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142000" :question/id #uuid "949bd398-6573-53d2-bf2d-21cf0dde3f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-142000" :question/problem "![](images/98/98edb404419e7ab515109f87addb44709513007b1a0105b648a3ce2b62ad547f.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+1=4.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "ab992999-a43c-5b0c-874e-f97040b58cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" :answer/id #uuid "91869c0b-2488-53b8-980c-0c2c402ce0f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/671723d87f1a67d9aa6a1f954b934e271d81eedfb75a65037fca3403ebebfd96" :answer/id #uuid "d0aa5750-a42b-5232-a712-34850cd9b3f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer/id #uuid "9e0d1de6-b1c8-5a40-bc71-a155680b07fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "6f9abc86-74e1-5d19-8f4f-0f0e7a56d821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a33bc7f4-158e-59b4-b555-27008daa9757" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/671723d87f1a67d9aa6a1f954b934e271d81eedfb75a65037fca3403ebebfd96" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :answer-field/correct "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669" :question/id #uuid "d39218d1-1972-5152-bee8-516235be3a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-143669" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f86984919b15283134e1b3a9479ff8c79ec8dfacc84975e82f88704b7b26dd3a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is  $B-2D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=4.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{9}{4}$ unit down. Therefore, $D=-\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, $B-2D=4-2\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{4})=4+\\frac{9}{2}=\\frac{17}{2}.$  \n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149766/ma-source-field/b616f07b8bb2f51a5122f18013ea2d3f445a374797d1f0805f2f59536458ac28/b84fd199de02d074681f284eb5fe7f2e716d60e640d03dab08be8c2ffb95c521" :answer/id #uuid "efe97fc4-e92a-5171-a755-91e261820e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149766/ma-source-field/b616f07b8bb2f51a5122f18013ea2d3f445a374797d1f0805f2f59536458ac28/f34afcd1d8d