a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4xz) \\\\  & =2x-z+4x \\\\  & =6x-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(6x-z)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,6x-z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162583/ma-source-field/d3eaa4a41879e4fcc24147adc77c2dd1e6b6d7b864d7190c049b1f450aece74c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a3fd63f-9991-5781-b4f8-9c4b0abc65ec"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" :answer/id #uuid "61124a49-e750-5eed-9f63-4fab70f48c25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" :answer/id #uuid "282a04d7-5121-553a-8c70-66602f8c83db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" :answer/id #uuid "8d1b7514-50b8-5ddd-9dc3-5b90007cd7cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/e046adedf89f81d289022d153f88fca288761f35fcfa1e156567c491565c6452" :answer/id #uuid "4a1c8270-8fd2-50fc-8447-30acc60e9312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" :answer/id #uuid "bfa1654c-e948-5fc3-a89a-4fe52cc8fccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "4112b8f8-a1d3-5ca1-a272-50f00bc81e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/e046adedf89f81d289022d153f88fca288761f35fcfa1e156567c491565c6452" "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c"] :answer-field/correct "q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162644" :question/id #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162644" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b69485bc-fe91-5715-a1be-f3a4cae4eec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "43d7fcb0-ff70-592c-ad54-21abfd7d0ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1d2fdced-3009-5582-9920-2ae6deb17073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "5b5ce768-561a-530a-b18b-d90e38f2f278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "0fd4e3aa-8ad0-50a4-8f3f-5869b4c7e1f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea34e434-1d65-55e5-98c8-c4dc723100a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :answer-field/correct "q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-163839" :question/id #uuid "7c94f5db-a52d-5269-9d70-48b35e30ba08" :question/math-academy-id "q-163839" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b99ff5d9d55de34b2cb3e2176e7c4171a5583e1e010626796c3ca2f9d9ed29cb.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above.\nWhat is the global maximum of the function?" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global maximum of a function is the largest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global maximum.\n\n- A global maximum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global maximum. There can be zero, one, or many global maximum points.\n\nFor our function, the maximum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=10.$ Therefore, the global maximum is $10.$ The function reaches this value at both $(x,y)=(2,4)$ and $(x,y)=(-4,4).$\n\n![](images/bf/bf82159ccb39f6c07fa870abe04911847dcbb240bd1cf5e6be8a1216fa9cf327.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-163839/ma-source-field/ea9ffa88664de0a2376f44eaee4f19c68aa270d4270e5d2cc27bb9cff2c0478e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ee9cbe8-ad40-5155-b42d-1802f36adf27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-163839"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164249/ma-source-field/dc960a14ed09c1214ef941ee7f398c7b05bb4639b061ddfd2c4c857100bb5592/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "dd6ec8be-4e28-5339-a7f2-8fd7158128e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164249/ma-source-field/dc960a14ed09c1214ef941ee7f398c7b05bb4639b061ddfd2c4c857100bb5592/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "99ff0be