/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :answer-field/correct "q-164249/ma-source-field/dc960a14ed09c1214ef941ee7f398c7b05bb4639b061ddfd2c4c857100bb5592/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164249" :question/id #uuid "16dea1c4-5f05-52d5-8897-db965a563c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164249" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z & =12 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}-4z+4) & =12+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}={4}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164249/ma-source-field/dc960a14ed09c1214ef941ee7f398c7b05bb4639b061ddfd2c4c857100bb5592"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164249"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/cc3b771d69c249b43b6611d0bc746155921a411fbf43e84f275766a62a6727d8" :answer/id #uuid "6feba394-c3ca-5316-a6b7-e7c023aefbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/d4d9d0c58dac6fecb6615f55a16d9d3e84ce77e12a45bac652d7b13344a08019" :answer/id #uuid "d8d770c7-1de6-53fa-b478-f0ede460b35e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/625f40a59af0f5938119dbedf38d07692ba9d02d04e5cf360117ecca1c5ee729" :answer/id #uuid "e422031f-1484-5bc6-8b3c-a582a65649b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/a45b3d817136e66dedc99befbbdb23cc00480a3166e8ebd3be46752fa9cd57d5" :answer/id #uuid "1b1a5a20-c7b4-5185-92b5-163b7a139d28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/6e8d353a8a5dc51a4e32f114b42e5f84c440535e0c2eb2babb272216706a7979" :answer/id #uuid "cb516869-a543-5bb4-a49a-1d6a41dfce68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e" :answer-field/id #uuid "79567a05-b827-5460-9e1f-fb9fcfce3867" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/cc3b771d69c249b43b6611d0bc746155921a411fbf43e84f275766a62a6727d8" "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/d4d9d0c58dac6fecb6615f55a16d9d3e84ce77e12a45bac652d7b13344a08019" "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/625f40a59af0f5938119dbedf38d07692ba9d02d04e5cf360117ecca1c5ee729" "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/a45b3d817136e66dedc99befbbdb23cc00480a3166e8ebd3be46752fa9cd57d5" "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/6e8d353a8a5dc51a4e32f114b42e5f84c440535e0c2eb2babb272216706a7979"] :answer-field/correct "q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e/cc3b771d69c249b43b6611d0bc746155921a411fbf43e84f275766a62a6727d8" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164412" :question/id #uuid "75aa15a4-a235-5132-bf56-78143897ca7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164412" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the parabolic cylinder $3(x+2)^{2}=6(y+3)$ and the plane $z=4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a parabola. What is the vertex of the parabola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=4,$ we substitute $z=4$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+2)^{2} & =6(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =2(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xy$-plane with the vertex at $(-2,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abbeda26-2fc0-5195-be26-ae79c72fc7bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/a987209810d6edcb3ab559f4b60755221d595b556581783dc3fd53282b7021dc" :answer/id #uuid "de5685b5-e86e-5a26-8d7a-36145d147fe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{5}{2},-6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/4b98e5e78091b02e518564cb3b6e020fa88df47506cc02777a196c239e11d4a2" :answer/id #uuid "26585b8c-e264-5ec5-9955-637ca3eab6f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(14,30)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/7bc944bf24568286d29244a96b94a160809ef74112971aaa27ac9396663d0d75" :answer/id #uuid "5225db26-fbee-5e92-ab23-1c2785ab7665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{11}{2},12)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/f91c35ab495519a0169ef8964eb1610d3f1fd5449d07730b49ea53165686b6c1" :answer/id #uuid "1e4aa85c-9ff1-574b-86fb-ac6e431fa3ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(-\\frac{5}{2},-6)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/613d6d91b0fda088c6f8ed6ca412a77d1f1e5560b26f35f2cbea40502f470d70" :answer/id #uuid "8ffd5745-f4c8-5a19-adc0-b37920b54995" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(\\frac{11}{2},12)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499" :answer-field/id #uuid "7805dc28-4db0-584d-a7f0-aae461b099c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/a987209810d6edcb3ab559f4b60755221d595b556581783dc3fd53282b7021dc" "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/4b98e5e78091b02e518564cb3b6e020fa88df47506cc02777a196c239e11d4a2" "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/7bc944bf24568286d29244a96b94a160809ef74112971aaa27ac9396663d0d75" "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/f91c35ab495519a0169ef8964eb1610d3f1fd5449d07730b49ea53165686b6c1" "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/613d6d91b0fda088c6f8ed6ca412a77d1f1e5560b26f35f2cbea40502f470d70"] :answer-field/correct "q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499/a987209810d6edcb3ab559f4b60755221d595b556581783dc3fd53282b7021dc" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165039" :question/id #uuid "29b73a1c-11c1-5790-9fa9-ce94ade43d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-165039" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}+4t,3{t}^{2}+9t⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}+4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}+9t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t+4,6t+9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c⟨1,3⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c⟨1,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨3t+4,6t+9⟩ & =c⟨1,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨3t+4,6t+9⟩ & =⟨c,3c⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3t+4=c \\\\ 6t+9=3c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain that $c=3t+4.$ Substituting $c=3t+4$ into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t+9 & =3(3t+4) \\\\ 6t+9 & =9t+12 \\\\ 3t & =-3 \\\\ t & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $⟨1,3⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=-1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1) & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}+4(-1),3(-1)^{2}+9(-1)⟩=⟨-\\frac{5}{2},-6⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨1,3⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(-\\frac{5}{2},-6).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165039/ma-source-field/657c384140b2a4c629052c10c7bc4d010d4c353a511a927bd50600c876db6499"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4636870-89db-5bf9-8a04-777407957e33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {