q-331263/ma-source-field/bc777f7984b499c5693dcaecdebb80f2a7c4f197b6ec5cd5b5e17d9a93416088/cfed2861e58b14bd32791afe9b695f6e171131d07ad8f792380dafa1ca75782d" "q-331263/ma-source-field/bc777f7984b499c5693dcaecdebb80f2a7c4f197b6ec5cd5b5e17d9a93416088/a75ec584caab4f91a0157b3c7dafab6e35036d801c110f7d6e7353315f7408c1" "q-331263/ma-source-field/bc777f7984b499c5693dcaecdebb80f2a7c4f197b6ec5cd5b5e17d9a93416088/0740002e6dd32be292369d2073cdb3b10001f09e62fab6969da323795777f30f"] :answer-field/correct "q-331263/ma-source-field/bc777f7984b499c5693dcaecdebb80f2a7c4f197b6ec5cd5b5e17d9a93416088/9884b3d4561f984b9f74d4dfbc46d638d6d0d2526a39089343db9a03d7b278d1" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331263" :question/id #uuid "bd84d2d8-6305-5ac3-8cd6-a34b4f857553" :question/math-academy-id "q-331263" :question/problem "![](images/26/26f5b15d20d9f57ee9b1d396683dd4dbad06a656b579ac0fd81241d362a28569.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/9f/9fb8c20672705e9d68e69d32e7ff3499ec71560e10aa85136b3f3ad75c5fb5ed.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we reflect $y=u(t)$ in the $y$-axis, which gives $y=u(-t).$\n\n- Next, we shift by two units to the right, giving $y=u(-(t-2))=u(2-t).$\n\n- Finally, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=2u(2-t).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=2u(2-t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331263/ma-source-field/bc777f7984b499c5693dcaecdebb80f2a7c4f197b6ec5cd5b5e17d9a93416088"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "253b1011-a313-5004-8cbe-61133586e6b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/123942cd749876c17a6b2111c522f57d2f90392a6bbce40d0548fb0c6e09c0bf" :answer/id #uuid "24fd7005-9776-5c47-b5c3-2edac4af6f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/0a09441f4183675937fd5c7d25dc74c984d4215bff154f382c148de72daff13c" :answer/id #uuid "32566370-0baa-5fb1-b7f3-81b3affe8868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{(s-3)(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/0bb036e6f9e3ade09811ac7a129d6d153604bcdb525df124b120017cec66a044" :answer/id #uuid "0716fd91-169b-5f0b-a6f5-08943732d486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s-1)(s+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/fe8e7e9d97ee2c82ec4b022a5376bac5592f847974d7c031c043b4432cb41f51" :answer/id #uuid "da50ab10-42e1-5cd7-9d4f-7393d8b338d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/9a58e8520188fa184cb9883a40850d11225e6ed1205009948338b9bd5632466b" :answer/id #uuid "47701396-f6b7-5c19-a7f4-3d458bef5ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s+1}{(s-3)(s+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a417b69-1171-54da-bd75-777eee884877" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/123942cd749876c17a6b2111c522f57d2f90392a6bbce40d0548fb0c6e09c0bf" "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/0a09441f4183675937fd5c7d25dc74c984d4215bff154f382c148de72daff13c" "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/0bb036e6f9e3ade09811ac7a129d6d153604bcdb525df124b120017cec66a044" "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/fe8e7e9d97ee2c82ec4b022a5376bac5592f847974d7c031c043b4432cb41f51" "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/9a58e8520188fa184cb9883a40850d11225e6ed1205009948338b9bd5632466b"] :answer-field/correct "q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0/fe8e7e9d97ee2c82ec4b022a5376bac5592f847974d7c031c043b4432cb41f51" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331457" :question/id #uuid "fde1c354-d593-5da3-9167-ee1bf6674333" :question/math-academy-id "q-331457" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{3t}-{e}^{-t}$ for $s>3.$" :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{-t}} & =L{{e}^{3t}}+L{-{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+1},\\,s>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{3t}}-L{{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(s+1)-(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1-s+3}{(s-3)(s+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(s-3)(s+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-1,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{f(t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-1,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331457/ma-source-field/913297b3b23df07d1ca57c9a405d246b01775038a418172c48ed572211933bb0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ad93e2e-20ab-5179-90b2-f96a357bd94c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120248 :question/answer-fields 17592186117617] {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/e336f34dbaf1fa6f82e0085208e000e22d99dead9bb6ec9bacc47968aa86e62a" :answer/id #uuid "cbf33e14-d217-5957-83e1-d43d4854445a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/d1014c3b89fa16147087f3cf34ee892fe2126f1cb5b8e3d8e0e6d07671c9b099" :answer/id #uuid "d2f7e9c3-d0a4-5c14-ad36-84ce7ce201f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/6752e17097f799416eda38d375be7f7edefdcdefa1bac5adb4a5dc8f8b29e5c1" :answer/id #uuid "6a162c78-4b2f-5cb3-bbfc-9d6ac2a6eb14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/0a3f2fdc622369df0cd849230eedcd4b4cb11f46733e1d2af9c3fcca69fc319c" :answer/id #uuid "1b3ad161-64a2-5b71-ad24-c120e8ec6285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/5a65408d9c616b2430efb0c8cb2ab532728ae3bcdab95c0e7dd032f37f6dd1b3" :answer/id #uuid "9b7e3c75-5535-5316-bea0-bf6c928449b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}\\,j-\\frac{3}{5}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffbf219-9fc7-55d4-a011-546b8183375e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/e336f34dbaf1fa6f82e0085208e000e22d99dead9bb6ec9bacc47968aa86e62a" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/d1014c3b89fa16147087f3cf34ee892fe2126f1cb5b8e3d8e0e6d07671c9b099" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/6752e17097f799416eda38d375be7f7edefdcdefa1bac5adb4a5dc8f8b29e5c1" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/0a3f2fdc622369df0cd849230eedcd4b4cb11f46733e1d2af9c3fcca69fc319c" "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/5a65408d9c616b2430efb0c8cb2ab532728ae3bcdab95c0e7dd032f37f6dd1b3"] :answer-field/correct "q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7/e336f34dbaf1fa6f82e0085208e000e22d99dead9bb6ec9bacc47968aa86e62a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "fee02912-87a3-5a99-92ba-f8ae9f270c88"] :question/problem "The equations of a curve $r(t)$ and its corresponding unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at an arbitrary point are given below. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at the point $P(0,3,4).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ) \\\\ T(t) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,3,4)$ on the given curve. We know that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,3,4⟩ \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+3\\text{ }j+4\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components of $i$, $j$, and $k$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=3 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,3,4)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{16}{25}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,3,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=\\frac{-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k}{1}=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =(-i)\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(i\\cdot j)+\\frac{4}{5}(i\\cdot k) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33233/ma-source-field/2cd93593a9780cc59b3ab1b9587eb55922bab59443714cf468fcf2d46746b7f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce" :answer/id #uuid "a16ca557-7a7d-5129-94ca-a6d1c29b2a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/0e1501d5d069b6a33e5fa6e65bf8b7a20ca58f1cee187a0b4ca4c5288d90195a" :answer/id #uuid "76fc81c1-1019-5d0d-b421-389e9c68eec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/98f64c562ab0076c4396accc98ed2c6ad7a2b47f590d90708077aee1009c51ac" :answer/id #uuid "cd361f69-82b4-5f33-bc72-7eec188e73d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/362a78ff63cca1b390872b8d740139a8d440d84db8a21afe8440a2b4d309b91a" :answer/id #uuid "73d2ca92-0022-5ad8-b7a5-3fa9671b330a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/4049222731792196becc45836650a3fe3622f5af63b26fd7dd68f0b75cd4fb0c" :answer/id #uuid "e0742820-f0eb-53a8-82b6-8737f0d716be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0060aa3-58d9-54a6-9803-caa490ce4163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce" "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/0e1501d5d069b6a33e5fa6e65bf8b7a20ca58f1cee187a0b4ca4c5288d90195a" "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/98f64c562ab0076c4396accc98ed2c6ad7a2b47f590d90708077aee1009c51ac" "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/362a78ff63cca1b390872b8d740139a8d440d84db8a21afe8440a2b4d309b91a" "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/4049222731792196becc45836650a3fe3622f5af63b26fd7dd68f0b75cd4fb0c"] :answer-field/correct "q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74/557e18a252614e3998f5ed29942cee75951396ec4308d0139b0693816f6128ce" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332591" :question/id #uuid "cdbef393-ee24-56cd-abfd-6178ddb5b54d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332591" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332591/ma-source-field/4fbdee38626b1b5c6621e39397a07c8ba325a95b468bad258b1c3ca6f380ae74"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eecbfc4-f7eb-5d4c-bea6-8fd21839804c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332595/ma-source-field/35967