f0fd2a3/cf254897122e2a3c5f71830ccc993e056ef540796582d394b48853f3fd652130"] :answer-field/correct "q-332739/ma-source-field/a3853248f42a3ca7865133e29857b44cb38cd8ccacd4f40762d854529f0fd2a3/3f4e79c682aafa58cf2256897c94c721463b3413a457de8bd1187b097f89a9cc" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332739" :question/id #uuid "b74c0fe3-3f12-5992-93c1-45a8876eedf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-332739" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution has the same exponential factor, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332739/ma-source-field/a3853248f42a3ca7865133e29857b44cb38cd8ccacd4f40762d854529f0fd2a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:know