ed}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e404c6-f4b3-5b21-aedc-a9e73b49a00d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/19253c3abb42c14e51b5cde6280e99c5ec639c6b18647f3eb335ebfee9eecb6d" "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/e220447e9b4c9fb01eae852e0985e7c35f79563172a21838c32d3619a87f64bc" "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/2ebbd3e84d03ae44e2413decc36a783de58d33ab783acb18945dfd8b3fd195f9" "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/853a9260b79598b81fa7b18393509d38fad7aeff210198622c2edd9ed48f3164" "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/9711d46aace8153c43ca9814c1ec0100882c4ce4ee5a7bcdb0ddc9980ce75f72"] :answer-field/correct "q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f/853a9260b79598b81fa7b18393509d38fad7aeff210198622c2edd9ed48f3164" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "b57e3584-dab2-5078-9ba7-3beaafafb71c"] :question/problem "Find a basis of ${H}^{⊥}$ if $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vector that spans the subspace $H$ as ${h}_{1}.$ \n\nA vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to ${H}^{⊥}$ if $x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {h}_{1}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwith the augmented matrix $M,$ which is already in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one), so ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{2}-\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3}.$ \nSo, every vector in ${H}^{⊥}$ has the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{2}-\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of ${H}^{⊥}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39953/ma-source-field/6e895b4ab79796aa9366bb4f2f90ce9331af5b3369642f169acc46b18a963d7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/de3b684342615eb42bd3fd791082af53f5ed14a4c85c1274c82199581db3ef5e" :answer/id #uuid "c978c2b1-ccc1-54be-9587-b2edd6ded6df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/410e2dc125509aee85f6bb48fa5e5495ef0e380ffb00773fbc223639c4077898" :answer/id #uuid "6b8c038e-f611-5478-9aa9-a2bfda5d0840" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/4e0c847f7ac76b7ca11f25a5d6df01b04c62fd7268be753dc15c7f8325c318eb" :answer/id #uuid "4ae28e12-3029-507c-ade0-f3e66e2e8d28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/43302fc5fb707030f40212d8c4d09f51198eefbd417f1e4b1248861c1969b11b" :answer/id #uuid "5fe5ff4c-e5fc-5063-9a2a-2461632dec52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/2f05b45e93be56ad2633f42704ce90bf93b6d876be7ee43dc16e2fe54b7d6a35" :answer/id #uuid "cb465645-5781-56a6-9ef8-8bcad739b465" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040" :answer-field/id #uuid "c97e3a1a-a6d7-5da5-9304-dedf20c2e8e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/de3b684342615eb42bd3fd791082af53f5ed14a4c85c1274c82199581db3ef5e" "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/410e2dc125509aee85f6bb48fa5e5495ef0e380ffb00773fbc223639c4077898" "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/4e0c847f7ac76b7ca11f25a5d6df01b04c62fd7268be753dc15c7f8325c318eb" "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/43302fc5fb707030f40212d8c4d09f51198eefbd417f1e4b1248861c1969b11b" "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/2f05b45e93be56ad2633f42704ce90bf93b6d876be7ee43dc16e2fe54b7d6a35"] :answer-field/correct "q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040/2f05b45e93be56ad2633f42704ce90bf93b6d876be7ee43dc16e2fe54b7d6a35" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40175" :question/id #uuid "daa0bc39-0770-52e4-a043-5e620f02bd66" :question/math-academy-id "q-40175" :question/problem "Find a basis of $\\,\\text{Ker}(T)$ given that $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-6x+y \\\\ 12x-2y\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Finding the kernel of $\\,T\\,$ is equivalent to finding the null space of the standard matrix of $\\,T.$\n\nFor the given linear transformation, the standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 12 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSetting $x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],$ we then need to solve the equation $Tx=0.$ First, we reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 12 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{6}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, if $x\\in \\text{Ker}(T),$ then \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]y,\\,y\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of $\\text{Ker}(T).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40175/ma-source-field/d7a69b0c73d07293ceda4df419b54c824fb2f958e62fd7da56d323f63abcd040"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a60cd4e9-d478-52ef-871e-fb08ff3d68a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134324 :question/answer-fields 17592186131953] {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "60d24f5c-d76c-58b7-8bb9-8de74e9c53a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "3e05bfa4-b8d5-5314-9896-1644fc12c8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "106232b9-da3b-58f0-a9ad-aeb1d72e61ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "d8c8c952-741b-540c-ae4f-1f2228adddbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "3f35435b-3ec7-5129-a532-9c8f56441232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "fcba6dad-25cc-5f9d-90fd-fd2dcba2cca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :answer-field/correct "q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "246d48c4-ce2d-5de1-bae4-f0a5be4d4035"] :question/problem "$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}],\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\\,,[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nSuppose that $V=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ Given that $B$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{10}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{15}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{46}{46}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40818/ma-source-field/c2d71becd00e69ae4cf22d92986669afa1d0c4ee16fd33faead6f763deba26ba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-46423/ma-source-field/ef46ba0de2236c63a4a4b8a77d3ec36cc8e0891e6dfebec0cd41861fe3d18092/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "25e09f7a-29af-53a4-9a4e-2520091baf5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46423/ma-source-field/ef46ba0de2236c63a4a4b8a77d3ec36cc8e0891e6dfebec0cd41861fe3d18092/ed46a7ab66f4e1f0492ab8ee0b3b7d22df7bff44011d5a9f713d6c9393035ddc" :answer/id #uuid "6251f85c-171a-5a16-b27e-38d67d00cf84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46423/ma-source-field/ef46ba0de2236c63a4a4b8a77d3ec36cc8e0891e6dfebec0cd41861fe3d18092/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "ec41b2aa-2ae1-5a06-a1d9-3164f01e91c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46423/ma-source-field/ef46ba0de2236c63a4a4b8a77d3ec36cc8e0891e6dfebec0cd41861fe3d18092/7845f5bf94