/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "3e04bc45-f34f-56fc-9a0e-8643597c4852"] :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50148/ma-source-field/af8207d7cb15cf9b264f494c523ef136c9ac9b180a6f231e94e2c04b17b54426"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186097311 :question/answer-fields 17592186095760] {:db/id "q-50202/ma-source-field/d54072a16f099b2b76723a2083a4b2545b899864f703a6aa1b916ab904356b56/0ac3df8c3d05374c7e5b2debe08b07de986201fa711bb34fcad1dd2976d1c8c1" :answer/id #uuid "63e6049b-3fa6-56d6-be3f-051da1756c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-⟨{e}^{t}-4t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50202/ma-source-field/d54072a16f099b2b76723a2083a4b2545b899864f703a6aa1b916ab904356b56/721ae82c03cf66de2d84acc92a78e39644db115e5e39c0fa47da95cadb5ece36" :answer/id #uuid "e9edbf5b-46e4-5cd0-b404-b3646d7dc3ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "