academy-id "q-75002" :question/problem "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-9{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75002/ma-source-field/4e6e751fc9c0e1316b1dfd481881a2c88611ca72b1d769a4268e5dd7c743ecfb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c70963f-589d-532b-9286-559f68693df7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/a44378ee17b469e76e7bee3ed8a669cfd07ca3f863f9860c180cf2fc6a5b9581" :answer/id #uuid "b2c8946a-4d9c-52a7-8ae5-4aed16ff115e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/0e682956089fc6d7ef52c60c385754a0ee0dc402251e7058c94df0474e3637cc" :answer/id #uuid "37d0671e-8d90-5723-bec1-5a12ea0b3af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/377f4627f244a9d8642628dd0b4cdd216ca7322e6499411a6f2c37ee0938e6f6" :answer/id #uuid "6303f09f-c02d-5180-8d58-7e3433d694f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/251a464ae89d0cfe32dc1506e302f553b47a6e40ef3d9bb28b74aef772d8f35d" :answer/id #uuid "7239b56e-96c9-5c55-913c-7e31672cc705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67" :answer/id #uuid "1fb09896-278b-51c5-bd41-98eac88317a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "5acbcbd4-a6f5-5bca-971a-8de2b8094901" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/a44378ee17b469e76e7bee3ed8a669cfd07ca3f863f9860c180cf2fc6a5b9581" "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/0e682956089fc6d7ef52c60c385754a0ee0dc402251e7058c94df0474e3637cc" "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/377f4627f244a9d8642628dd0b4cdd216ca7322e6499411a6f2c37ee0938e6f6" "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/251a464ae89d0cfe32dc1506e302f553b47a6e40ef3d9bb28b74aef772d8f35d" "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67"] :answer-field/correct "q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5/0e682956089fc6d7ef52c60c385754a0ee0dc402251e7058c94df0474e3637cc" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75024" :question/id #uuid "3d8eef93-735e-5ee8-8363-b800d4ca0ad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-75024" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4},$ where ${x}_{2},$ ${x}_{3},$ and ${x}_{4}$ are free variables. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{4} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75024/ma-source-field/357d1e60ce5d27c246fb7dee7683b69b06e22289bdaea89949531d3f21eea3e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fd5a675-c692-505e-900b-d7500fb7c653"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/6b7e07594c8480d7ff7c3b053b30beff09b309eb8e24fcdd35f2f542c523b790" :answer/id #uuid "b819787d-2c96-52cd-8d8f-6fb4bd9fa32b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7d0ccb764d2ad99de3d761c0baaa0ded4458bdb6abaef988238/dfc9de37f8d4b24e7fa4cf8ab473312db52fba663b2a4e0577ccf1a5366c1d0d" :answer/id #uuid "9774ab3d-acd2-523f-9cda-0c0a39ef61d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75025/ma-source-field/1166a66061b1a7