answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "e1694262-cdf1-5325-9fc5-66702cda46da"] :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\,,\\,\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}⟩,$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{t}\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}\\,,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨{e}^{t}\\,,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0\\cdot {e}^{t}+1\\cdot \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}} & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only solution is $t=0.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{e}^{0}\\,,\\,\\sqrt{1+{0}^{2}}⟩=⟨1\\,,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨0\\,,\\,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75519/ma-source-field/f2b38d9347a2ab25fa90f6fe8c865aeb849922a7eebdfa3eea066496651252e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/77a913a5c68cf3d8de28dce3d3292b3a50a20caba1be6fc314343612f38e3ea2" :answer/id #uuid "c64155b0-249e-5565-ad41-5aa4d4de25a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/1fdb8dac9a33dff264a1441282384e6955f0294f914b3dca92b4510aa009c220" :answer/id #uuid "363b9e46-0e55-5119-8918-a99ef9c17cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/11948535861c8c617e49fd529fda48f2eb79ab2c4a2ee95d05f38328117ef743" :answer/id #uuid "7db323bd-027d-5a72-8744-915dc9466d84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/cbf73d33747e7378dc321a3a36a200c81edd3097e93e1a1f09c97cdfaea27c83" :answer/id #uuid "5bd9f381-647a-53f8-8916-ebcaa02fb734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/92ceb4efdc0cd986fcf6d914c334e6bc24d60c60afe74f5d1910588d4d342e77" :answer/id #uuid "ab114369-abaf-5996-96e1-bc98ccf909b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad20513b-7f6b-51c1-b3e8-54f31e6cfac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/77a913a5c68cf3d8de28dce3d3292b3a50a20caba1be6fc314343612f38e3ea2" "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/1fdb8dac9a33dff264a1441282384e6955f0294f914b3dca92b4510aa009c220" "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/11948535861c8c617e49fd529fda48f2eb79ab2c4a2ee95d05f38328117ef743" "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/cbf73d33747e7378dc321a3a36a200c81edd3097e93e1a1f09c97cdfaea27c83" "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/92ceb4efdc0cd986fcf6d914c334e6bc24d60c60afe74f5d1910588d4d342e77"] :answer-field/correct "q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97/77a913a5c68cf3d8de28dce3d3292b3a50a20caba1be6fc314343612f38e3ea2" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76110" :question/id #uuid "bfd92570-bd08-5565-9c64-935de2ba2369" :question/math-academy-id "q-76110" :question/problem "![](images/76/760ddc657e8372a3860e2553e4f2b713a8b12544586c708e5f2c1922462567a8.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $y=f(x)$ above continuous? You may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram." :question/worked-solution "To determine the intervals of continuity of a function, we take the domain of the function and exclude any points of discontinuity.\n\nThe function is defined on the intervals $(-\\infty ,3),$  and $(3,\\infty ).$ There is a discontinuity at $x=3$  but this is already excluded.  \n\nThere is also a discontinuity at $x=-3,$ so we need to exclude that.\n\nTherefore, the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-3),$ $(-3,3),$  and $(3,\\infty ).$ It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals. \n\nAmong the answer choices, the correct one is the following:\n\n$\\,$ $(-2,3)$ \n\nNotice that:\n\n- $(-3,4)$ and $(0,5)$ contain the excluded point $x=3,$ so the function is not continuous on these intervals.\n\n- $(-\\infty ,-2)$ and  $(-\\infty ,0)$ contain the point of discontinuity $x=-3$, so the function is not continuous on these intervals." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76110/ma-source-field/253a5f36af83a0035576d9af980e33d26491daccdac76696453f54d027060d97"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e806aac-62fc-5c53-a15e-a2ce175dad25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76110"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76493/ma-source-field/0377ab3e5dd641539dc866f99444a1d036e11e75aa0d6a340c5a566a93bd19f1/7059834b1a1b560d2c8fabb05d2fc3dd7be46b3df7f81915af34e