e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78981" :question/id #uuid "4bb06435-9175-533a-8727-5e983d5d29c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-78981" :question/problem "For which value of $x$ does the function $f(x)=18x-2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}$ have a local maximum?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =18-6{x}^{2}-12x \\\\  & =-6({x}^{2}+2x-3) \\\\  & =-6(x-1)(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-6(x-1)(x+3)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-3,1.\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-4,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-4) & =-6(-4-1)(-4+3)=-30<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =-6(0-1)(0+3)=18>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-6(2-1)(2+3)=-30<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $-3$ | $(-3,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-4$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-3,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=-3$ is a local minimum.\n\n- At $x=1,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=1$ is a local maximum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has one local maximum at $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-78981/ma-source-field/8528a2c7f5cd2c762663e26bd9ca51eef943d40586e7c5b403dc797767f9cf5b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33965139-0c6a-50fc-993a-e2acd6760212"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78981"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186184850 :question/answer-fields 17592186183679] {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "51e08aac-9339-503c-9a66-b74268d4d2f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "03fedd1c-29b4-5722-b1e7-b3c046e5b66c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "081bfb29-fde1-5481-b123-8eac743f086f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "6704d952-af2f-5f8a-a722-c90281d08d85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "a2ce8598-f6eb-5e70-b2e5-0d95b7a5f429" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d" :answer-field/id #uuid "1848e56b-8e02-510d-9f75-0f28e4f3c082" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :answer-field/correct "q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d92d6b12-34ec-5e74-a8fa-e75755bbf55a"] :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae6a514e0d9cde3db3c3b1dfa94e3804b5469dd5fb99b40a94684e88b573ec38.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units up. Hence, $D=3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+3=6.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)+3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79188/ma-source-field/19b6f4801d73ea8edadf31d084caa9db6f8f6054fd01d237821af3f52140408d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/a457cbc8e8f6bc1a9285b5150b046f82a66b52ae9e5552acd246736432c70d1f" :answer/id #uuid "1b9be70b-8bba-5dbc-9874-9d41aef0df8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/604e0a67320a59d8fbb8672d382c92fe490b634a2193108ccfdbeeecad061fd3" :answer/id #uuid "02fe5e77-2ad2-5965-be92-a482e775a25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/fcd32f74ec33961a2e758326a3db6dad3c2fac3b4b27772a4354d832285fd55f" :answer/id #uuid "e8082951-c2e2-5bd4-ae4c-cc8f0ae927ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/17a585f7e449097654e6203a1cecfc345eb0add5b0dd21896ece23319aa2c53b" :answer/id #uuid "f68d2bbb-4e6c-5bd4-90b2-31795bf23e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/4fec99fc4a9141173b3054423d799014cbb82993957d0c6202f115942207fce7" :answer/id #uuid "b15e42d6-24dd-593e-83e9-c56ca0fd1fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa048650-e823-530b-9d23-02d20a7d69e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/a457cbc8e8f6bc1a9285b5150b046f82a66b52ae9e5552acd246736432c70d1f" "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/604e0a67320a59d8fbb8672d382c92fe490b634a2193108ccfdbeeecad061fd3" "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/fcd32f74ec33961a2e758326a3db6dad3c2fac3b4b27772a4354d832285fd55f" "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/17a585f7e449097654e6203a1cecfc345eb0add5b0dd21896ece23319aa2c53b" "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/4fec99fc4a9141173b3054423d799014cbb82993957d0c6202f115942207fce7"] :answer-field/correct "q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f/604e0a67320a59d8fbb8672d382c92fe490b634a2193108ccfdbeeecad061fd3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79494" :question/id #uuid "dcd4b923-bea2-5168-a3b2-3077cdbbb018" :question/math-academy-id "q-79494" :question/problem "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion, is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the particle is initially at the origin with a velocity of $3\\,\\text{m/s},$ find the amplitude of the oscillation." :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written as\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the amplitude, and $ϕ$ is the phase. In our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=81\\,⟹\\,\\omega =9.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9t+ϕ).\n$$\n\nWe're given the initial condition $y(0)=0.$ Substituing this into the equation gives\n\n$$\nR\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=0\\,⟹\\,ϕ=0.\n$$\n\nSo our general solution reduces to\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the velocity is $3\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0,$ which means that ${y}^{′}(0)=3.$ Differentiating the general solution with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9R\\operatorname{cos}⁡9t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n3=9R\\,⟹\\,R=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the amplitude is $\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}.$ The solution for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79494/ma-source-field/69015cf029c32ae7dce0b3e9818d84e67803ad5c4c988441e324b8b99383186f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2dedcee-452d-50ff-844e-5648be3066b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79494"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/3f6a4b4b41807b3ea9dc091422129c9fe3ba523fa3f921893ccc88f9bf626cda" :answer/id #uuid "c8924757-c52d-5d0c-aeb8-9f98d7fe1fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,3,5,…,39},{51,53,55,…,99}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/226a27a43e12e92a24989a03295f59ba84db4a87bbb9ad19c0be1e5083816d82" :answer/id #uuid "39a47dc6-9573-5392-ae4c-e9ceaf0fea6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,3,5,…,49},{41,43,45,…,99}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/c8c307d16ed71eecf4e0b8c8a8ed64f1a2c1d56dd1023f05db6d9f653bf403e3" :answer/id #uuid "5ad4c8da-1a09-5685-a33c-1bcb1d28cc7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,3,5,…,49},{51,53,55,…,99}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/1a4d40c8b50542e39179d453f3bc838916aafce8d778175c39c7926386c7be91" :answer/id #uuid "cd19cb4f-0d4b-5559-8677-6233d145b1ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,3,5,…,69},{70,71,72,…,99}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/3d038e5f8cc673c45a5808666db769ca440923b7557f025ace2533055d25c7e2" :answer/id #uuid "0807d65c-c849-52a9-9b55-2038d785db97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{1,3,5,…,99},{2,4,6,…,98}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a" :answer-field/id #uuid "5326ac8e-fdd3-536f-93df-14753522f064" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/3f6a4b4b41807b3ea9dc091422129c9fe3ba523fa3f921893ccc88f9bf626cda" "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/226a27a43e12e92a24989a03295f59ba84db4a87bbb9ad19c0be1e5083816d82" "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/c8c307d16ed71eecf4e0b8c8a8ed64f1a2c1d56dd1023f05db6d9f653bf403e3" "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/1a4d40c8b50542e39179d453f3bc838916aafce8d778175c39c7926386c7be91" "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/3d038e5f8cc673c45a5808666db769ca440923b7557f025ace2533055d25c7e2"] :answer-field/correct "q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a/c8c307d16ed71eecf4e0b8c8a8ed64f1a2c1d56dd1023f05db6d9f653bf403e3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80432" :question/id #uuid "c61daa7e-9a16-5ba4-9cd7-641808843be0" :question/math-academy-id "q-80432" :question/problem "If $X={1,3,5,…,99}$, which collection of subsets of $X$ is a partition of $X?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{1,3,5,…,49},{51,53,55,…,99}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{1,3,5,…,99},{2,4,6,…,98}}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- ${{1,3,5,…,49},{41,43,45,…,99}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{1,3,5,…,69},{70,71,72,…,99}}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $70$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- ${{1,3,5,…,39},{51,53,55,…,99}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) do not appear in any subsets." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80432/ma-source-field/7eb99bcfad6b8ef78af2e614e0a312ff1b623a38055f8d99c9923d3d8b0c258a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2a9a1d-2d20-58cf-a1ee-bee2f4cf120d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80432"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186097376 :question/answer-fields 17592186096150] {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/a70c2c97dfddb48157f7e1bded34e55718b89a052d98a547e4479a8552a63481" :answer/id #uuid "8625a627-3b15-58cf-ba3e-833914e69b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3{t}^{3},\\,t{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/a5569616a1ed02f767e74efaca2b6ca05ebd9bec5e4db46627973ee226ba3966" :answer/id #uuid "57f28662-75ae-5e7c-a727-6cc70f2a946d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/0cad4a030334d7f1695574676ada61aea86080da4e6b3ce16c3d6bfd5666691e" :answer/id #uuid "980abdcc-03e8-5481-8470-6167a822e9b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3},\\,-t{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/ead16664da44e06a050b99b3fc34a90cc0f51d118559061e712a585454111ff5" :answer/id #uuid "f022a8e1-f660-5e62-989c-eb808fd735df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3},\\,-{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/f5582f15e975ccce03a51c356a333639e3a997c8594964b32d7fec992da7e89a" :answer/id #uuid "b1bda4bf-9a89-5c13-9d41-84a013832509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4c5d2d-c5b6-5ecd-b722-b08fb64f2522" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/a70c2c97dfddb48157f7e1bded34e55718b89a052d98a547e4479a8552a63481" "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/a5569616a1ed02f767e74efaca2b6ca05ebd9bec5e4db46627973ee226ba3966" "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/0cad4a030334d7f1695574676ada61aea86080da4e6b3ce16c3d6bfd5666691e" "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/ead16664da44e06a050b99b3fc34a90cc0f51d118559061e712a585454111ff5" "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/f5582f15e975ccce03a51c356a333639e3a997c8594964b32d7fec992da7e89a"] :answer-field/correct "q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5/f5582f15e975ccce03a51c356a333639e3a997c8594964b32d7fec992da7e89a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "22f82dbd-7046-58bc-9a39-900370a35623"] :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,{e}^{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80460/ma-source-field/4a3be1ed6e6a7dc5f01b2d7a4a834e8bd76c0d00544a8c9316158c5a55f08ab5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-80467/ma-source-field/3de1708500946b5b4069be057acc71002ee4ec56f4f8a266ceda0d99a56135d7/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" :answer/id #uuid "931df98b-abe6-5c33-9026-a64e621c7860" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80467/ma-source-field/3de1708500946b5b4069be057acc71002ee4ec56f4f8a266ceda0d99a56135d7/655ede254939c8720ff15fa47ebfaa58a37f5de0c0b757a45cc6bf14b9606903" :answer/id #uuid "4b30d639-ee9f-5dd6-a783-78b787a8dd54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80467/ma-source-field/3de1708500946b5b4069be057acc71002ee4ec56f4f8a266ceda0d99a56135d7/8492608054a267cc425c8eb3b5946844a2a80022f7b456ab2d9eae49c53be7f5" :answer/id #uuid "f91f8571-a85e-5261-a33d-4e0eb8050300" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80467/ma-source-field/3de1708500946b5b4069be057acc71002ee4ec56f4f8a266ceda0d99a56135d7/fe2a88bb40c84469c9d4347b9459a49a2043ff3a9a3fd859c6b18594ed560d4c" :answer/id #uuid "3a9bca69-8e29-54e8-841b-6cdbc