2a89" "q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01/608aa8eee889cc9ba516a8468964f58babe8f298be2aea159122552581473af6" "q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01/de61cabd6b263988b6c4eb8b6a195fa3de6877a4fc1e2d2a755ea1496347978a" "q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01/83ecf189389cf3fc70f0747c1da38769a48a4b0abd4fc8cd441b40be21951c93"] :answer-field/correct "q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01/de61cabd6b263988b6c4eb8b6a195fa3de6877a4fc1e2d2a755ea1496347978a" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80810" :question/id #uuid "fb01c25e-4ce1-591f-b1b8-8c295e973407" :question/math-academy-id "q-80810" :question/problem "Which statement is **not** true?" :question/worked-solution "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a natural number.  For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin N.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80810/ma-source-field/75632f6a3a952c667732f1e5141a52b1ee09576edfa7e1f75aac5f2e6cb8dc01"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80810"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "99a4d6e3-caf9-544f-ba67-8f950954be82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "b467a51e-f9be-5bed-89bc-7ff012c894de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "748a5bc0-46b6-5698-846f-66d6952f985d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "149698b5-3361-5f52-a32c-6ed656acfe8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "66613f28-b688-5af5-87c4-a12f46f9bd0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2967834-56c7-54af-a045-1eb688f37565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :answer-field/correct "q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80917" :question/id #uuid "8179a1bc-9dd2-5c9c-a7dd-3de3a7cd250c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80917" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ a\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince $A$ is upper-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5-5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5-5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+2{w}_{2}=1 \\\\ 0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{1}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{1}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{5t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80917/ma-source-field/8229ea581279db4b55bb24c0e8bf1faeaae4dda96f8a7f01ff1ebeb68828a563"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c19f9d9-fa4b-5261-b9a0-99a203aeac30"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80917"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80919/ma-source-field/e95bbc0cfaee06f0e97ea4c65ef9356967f9ca8973dccdff31da3593251f895f/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "6f01c0dd-442a-5b90-8b62-5974e56662f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80919/ma-source-field/e95bbc0cfaee06f0e97ea4c65ef9356967f9ca8973dccdff31da3593251f895f/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "eba8c50d-8cd6-567a-b472-75707ce03343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80919/ma-source-field/e95bbc0cfaee06f0e97ea4c65ef9356967f9ca8973dccdff31da3593251f895f/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "645e0e17-2268-567a-ac17-75ba1595de6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value