id "q-80919" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince $A$ is lower-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-1$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1+1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{2}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80919/ma-source-field/e95bbc0cfaee06f0e97ea4c65ef9356967f9ca8973dccdff31da3593251f895f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c19f9d9-fa4b-5261-b9a0-99a203aeac30"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80919"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4ccc94845abad1c93b4e6783c1ff134ba5ef122c4383cf62627335f410950/6a31f65bb59f4d06f9fa2eb5f4f195a05b617df56a4880ff57b02666922cf5eb" :answer/id #uuid "8249b093-9fe6-5147-b1d5-815d065e1a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧¬Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4ccc94845abad1c93b4e6783c1ff134ba5ef122c4383cf62627335f410950/bbb1cf4a106bf4367cc6beedd17f1625d08ffdd9eac3386366c949c303f9fe19" :answer/id #uuid "ca2a53ee-7270-5777-87a4-50b35f9c3e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(P∧Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4ccc94845abad1c93b4e6783c1ff134ba5ef122c4383cf62627335f410950/66421ed265c4c11f591792941e8cbb8df0de1d9edfb1686ec48731f0ddc1bb4b" :answer/id #uuid "bb42fe88-30ff-5d4a-9ddc-7267e2860a9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬(P∨Q)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4ccc94845abad1c93b4e6783c1ff134ba5ef122c4383cf62627335f410950/cc79b4ff5e57877b19c312bd528649c68f82425285d1dc55e0d1d7027dbdce04" :answer/id #uuid "a9e68e25-6dfe-5220-94ef-0f37adf8b6aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∨Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81372/ma-source-field/c1c4c