6416148" "q-84829/ma-source-field/ba8ac2e1498250f8444fc0328560f789a7a9930b27483d3a6ee5edb50276e745/981a2951e3fccc9ba81c501537ab818060069591c658c07fba6936fa5fd0dd27"] :answer-field/correct "q-84829/ma-source-field/ba8ac2e1498250f8444fc0328560f789a7a9930b27483d3a6ee5edb50276e745/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "d578c6cc-9bea-57a7-8928-c304b5f6c737"] :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=12y?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at the origin is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4(3)y.\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=3.$ Therefore, our parabola has its vertex at $(0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-84829/ma-source-field/ba8ac2e1498250f8444fc0328560f789a7a9930b27483d3a6ee5edb50276e745"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/05ac00bcc16d4b2d08ac9ab18e656edb2fa47a5aa8f633fe0f5a56559828843a" :answer/id #uuid "dae026cc-2f8b-57ac-b71d-10c48af3c603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/8f9ed2a91396b3e44a408bb97d7a3017a9918df3c39ce46a18b808c7085844e8" :answer/id #uuid "6242ac02-1910-5a41-abad-40594fc76cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/b0753e03decacc5945bd19d5138d477f578068100b51402d3fbfad4be36d087d" :answer/id #uuid "b7dae3f1-f3d4-52af-ab47-2cc200f1b13b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/78b0990d1ebcf3679ab040ab2b15a98499b03069551bfa6d44d1656e9dc76fad" :answer/id #uuid "2fff83ba-a026-5a48-a91c-bd58ef842ecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/a0715085b8cd9d31e7e81fd4fc47e4617263f8c98c2689afc5604b3b9993464c" :answer/id #uuid "624befe8-6b9c-5657-a58f-1250e92d2f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "c119d922-a10c-5cfb-9f5d-697a1f5368d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/05ac00bcc16d4b2d08ac9ab18e656edb2fa47a5aa8f633fe0f5a56559828843a" "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/8f9ed2a91396b3e44a408bb97d7a3017a9918df3c39ce46a18b808c7085844e8" "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/b0753e03decacc5945bd19d5138d477f578068100b51402d3fbfad4be36d087d" "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/78b0990d1ebcf3679ab040ab2b15a98499b03069551bfa6d44d1656e9dc76fad" "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/a0715085b8cd9d31e7e81fd4fc47e4617263f8c98c2689afc5604b3b9993464c"] :answer-field/correct "q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc/a0715085b8cd9d31e7e81fd4fc47e4617263f8c98c2689afc5604b3b9993464c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85966" :question/id #uuid "179e9be2-d5dc-5bf7-a08f-f77d3bd121bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-85966" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e03226558b1dbb2e93d23947b0b05f3d8413dc35207bbe9b536e68108f40955.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing by $3\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min},$ while the $5\\,\\text{cm}$ height does not change. If the volume of the rectangular prism is increasing at a rate of $15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min},$  how fast is its width changing when its dimensions are $6\\,\\text{cm}$ in length and $2\\,\\text{cm}$ in width?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ y & =2\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ z & =5\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-3\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=6\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $z=5\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSince $z$ is not changing and $z=5,$ we get\n\n$$\nV=5xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5xy) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =5x(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+5y(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =5(6)(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+5(2)(-3) \\\\ 15 & =30(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})-30 \\\\ 45 & =30(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the solid is increasing at a rate of $\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=6\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $z=5\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85966/ma-source-field/02147363dd5165963b01de568d88fcc9752058bba98457830e91392c037aa5fc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0cf1bf7-69a3-50b2-adaa-84982ffac95e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85966"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186079222 :question/answer-fields 17592186078080] {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3be8d0a7-6de2-5a8a-bb9b-dce0d9c14190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "2e9ae71a-f628-55f5-b849-79f13018ee74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "0355d7bc-5328-5a46-8f44-4dda5270bea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "43749bb5-2143-5e1c-a7a5-011564260c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "e998af51-e20b-5b84-bd4a-a9de461a347f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8309d1f3-a727-53df-8a35-d087b45480a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :answer-field/correct "q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "137cbf82-f6fa-5b07-a735-e5850a186305"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5x+6y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with one step to approximate $y(1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of \n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we add the initial condition data:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5x+6y \\\\  & =5\\cdot (0)+6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(6)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n| $1$ | $7$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86975/ma-source-field/fda760b918986e5b5a4c7733e797099c6eac497ebcfec7037e315e19cb9a4d6c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/399a1171be63caa83f3b05773062d220261fc0ca32bc76ca944970d42ebede7b" :answer/id #uuid "a30c29de-8bbd-5ce5-b082-0d86e79ae9ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/82c79a11c5f316588a4977bf9de059017422d38604e630b6407357df3b622d75" :answer/id #uuid "c4de3ee5-4e26-5981-b4bd-fa52650fe448" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/a51b5d98d135312d006e556f37cffdda39fee6cebfacdc46fdfba370ab35568c" :answer/id #uuid "ed0fd701-7b05-5e6d-9f51-cb1531e040d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/2a2dfa122b83e1fbc6b70be6ef717447914d5f79f3dfea05d917ce624c516d65" :answer/id #uuid "77d0fe15-2bfd-57f0-991d-684ad2dfd05b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/097bf54e53fd44fd496a8806d7ef0ea4f567d8a5a994b298b0fe8b19f4b98622" :answer/id #uuid "963f3713-419f-5a42-a8fd-36820ed2b9d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810" :answer-field/id #uuid "00acfb45-f915-59a3-94c8-f02ca6e1865b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/399a1171be63caa83f3b05773062d220261fc0ca32bc76ca944970d42ebede7b" "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/82c79a11c5f316588a4977bf9de059017422d38604e630b6407357df3b622d75" "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/a51b5d98d135312d006e556f37cffdda39fee6cebfacdc46fdfba370ab35568c" "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/2a2dfa122b83e1fbc6b70be6ef717447914d5f79f3dfea05d917ce624c516d65" "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/097bf54e53fd44fd496a8806d7ef0ea4f567d8a5a994b298b0fe8b19f4b98622"] :answer-field/correct "q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810/a51b5d98d135312d006e556f37cffdda39fee6cebfacdc46fdfba370ab35568c" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89417" :question/id #uuid "896ad0b2-d79e-5667-ae9b-69d97f290fa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-89417" :question/problem "Find an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this in the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4{x}_{3}-2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{3}=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89417/ma-source-field/5c13fae98de1ff91c50f6ee725cd8834f44b9082d897c8b937c57044251a9810"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4def2d61-0093-53cf-bcbb-1d2c3e6e1738"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89417"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186148213 :question/answer-fields 17592186147002] {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/76e98a77085f276070fce0f19a57521b91e5e35c504d4322a9778065298c7f4a" :answer/id #uuid "45721693-741e-5a77-adf1-966cec978820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(s-2)(s+4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/55b3ac8687427dfb5b75397138a575971471a4b41449f1562c111fcb2459e7eb" :answer/id #uuid "7c27cdcd-45ec-5582-8de2-98843f585000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/aae36ca6a1f1b5255a99035980bcd1495d2b8fcf3efd7f0c2b0e42d6861b7a2a" :answer/id #uuid "8662e7b5-1e0f-55ac-97f1-c70dd6d8b3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s-6}{(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/d2d3993b23a7c5a90d56873714b84c15d6c842e716ec63d8e15cc14b24fb0ddd" :answer/id #uuid "cecda9c9-be1d-5b87-8565-27cba4405226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{(s+2)(s-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/27fd4dd787eaf295db46ae1d5af5eaa525fe20d528090e3f5cc422ecfe418b66" :answer/id #uuid "6391f63d-2767-50fd-8d6d-399705dd193e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s+4}{(s-2)(s+4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135" :answer-field/id #uuid "b29f83ae-6ce7-5677-8e73-4e7762c39fa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/76e98a77085f276070fce0f19a57521b91e5e35c504d4322a9778065298c7f4a" "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/55b3ac8687427dfb5b75397138a575971471a4b41449f1562c111fcb2459e7eb" "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/aae36ca6a1f1b5255a99035980bcd1495d2b8fcf3efd7f0c2b0e42d6861b7a2a" "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/d2d3993b23a7c5a90d56873714b84c15d6c842e716ec63d8e15cc14b24fb0ddd" "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/27fd4dd787eaf295db46ae1d5af5eaa525fe20d528090e3f5cc422ecfe418b66"] :answer-field/correct "q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135/55b3ac8687427dfb5b75397138a575971471a4b41449f1562c111fcb2459e7eb" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "5620868a-e836-565c-a7cc-7e2d887588f3"] :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-2t}-{e}^{4t}$ for $s>4.$" :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{-2t}-{e}^{4t}} & =L{{e}^{-2t}}+L{-{e}^{4t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{-2t}}-L{{e}^{4t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following result:\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+2},\\,s>-2 \\\\ L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{-2t}}-L{{e}^{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+2}-\\frac{1}{s-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(s-4)-(s+2)}{(s+2)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{(s+2)(s-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{(s+2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{-2t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-2,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{4t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (4,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{f(t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(-2,\\infty )\\cap (4,\\infty )=(4,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89589/ma-source-field/54e4dc9b53794e6bbde2c433e7d53a284e4e1aa4c21c2f3a9e3ca85fafbec135"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94267/ma-source-field/f2abfd8c0cd7ce7e438b9319cd887998eea908ac2f80474a561dbc684e8cc41a/f59782668239e0f62ed502562c63af39a903d6166158656f77e2e77969a0ee25" :answer/id #uuid "f6f6cb90-2038-5a8d-9cb0-03bdb5ac61c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+16{y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94267/ma-source-field/f2abfd8c0cd7ce7e438b9319cd887998eea908ac2f80474a561dbc684e8cc41a/42cd03966ca63df58193e794feb9b2f29b2d3bd95422f79ab66fd09fa8709b59" :answer/id #uuid "0e31193a-a47b-5236-90bf-56a2004b1817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+8y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94267/ma-source-field/f2abfd8c0cd7ce7e438b9319cd887998eea908ac2f80474a561dbc684e8cc41a/2050771de2ea94095720b9cdfbc82a2699370003871d659a8a4f9d44b1efa388" :answer/id #uuid "7f5a553a-2376-55cd-bc5e-82413407a146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94267/ma-source-field/f2abfd8