t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing simple harmonic motion?" :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94267/ma-source-field/f2abfd8c0cd7ce7e438b9319cd887998eea908ac2f80474a561dbc684e8cc41a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bad79c3-d90e-5752-a3ea-381e9445ab15"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94267"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587/735ceb36c056ea9c83000cdb582d54ecbbc0d07b5065154bfe74793e26723a07" :answer/id #uuid "910cdfa2-d7b4-5e59-a5b6-0e5abae3d765" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587/a314f31d4dc48987ba33da88e455c71a4c35c39ec08d2650a2aab67fb8a51535" :answer/id #uuid "319779d2-534b-5610-b6a9-b434baf8c080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587/b93e53501cd2fc582b14c41183633e0325dcfb639ed84ddfda748648cf5d0fc2" :answer/id #uuid "46208be2-e44d-501e-b2d0-174fb33ac5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+8y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587/f8f967b9ba0dfd72e23a0625c740443c473c6497af883375facfecbc4fd94c2f" :answer/id #uuid "d9b7aa89-dd35-5e5d-85c6-68109bf39843" :answer/type :answer.type/ma