tion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=8\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2\\sqrt{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94268/ma-source-field/37b465be270b63bcdaefe7386ea0a46da6fdf633a513e97704902e9334aa5587"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bad79c3-d90e-5752-a3ea-381e9445ab15"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0be2561c-49b3-5f8b-ad20-1a5654de6657" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8a0438ff-3859-5e07-b762-c9106e8d2b52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "b44c6ba9-a1db-5d4e-b228-ff157e3abe87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "c9daf291-4613-5128-b807-55231aa6b7ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "2fe0ac12-3cc1-55d6-b9bf-ff24251e83b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d55ca46-1e37-53b2-a389-dff0a71c6234" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :answer-field/correct "q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94283" :question/id #uuid "3cf6d9af-b061-5993-b553-d544e56a866d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94283" :question/problem "The position $y(t),$ measured in meters, of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion, is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. Given that the particle is initially at the origin with a velocity of $4\\,\\text{m/s},$ find the amplitude of the oscillation." :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written as\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the amplitude, and $ϕ$ is the phase. In our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=8\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t+ϕ).\n$$\n\nWe're given the initial condition $y(0)=0.$ Substituing this into the equation gives\n\n$$\nR\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=0\\,⟹\\,ϕ=0.\n$$\n\nSo our general solution reduces to\n\n$$\ny=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t).\n$$\n\nWe're told that the velocity is $4\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0,$ which means that ${y}^{′}(0)=4.$ Differentiating the general solution with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2\\sqrt{2}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4=2\\sqrt{2}R\\,⟹\\,R=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the amplitude is $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.$ The solution for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94283/ma-source-field/6f304c73f19ec3f75c0f4bded21f2c4f058be8f76f6d61d8db0e07da47da8fbd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2dedcee-452d-50ff-844e-5648be3066b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94609/ma-source-field/7c3d1af2662a8686d500207febe06092bfdcfbd03b2e52ed5a2f7ca79194d9ef/3738af33e0fd2d882a3e9250568b27c422b80c25c0ec7c77bac037ac8d9f6e98" :answer/id #uuid "4dbc0f20-e5f6-5a52-a355-67a35255c6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94609/ma-source-field/7c3d1af2662a8686d500207febe06092bfdcfbd03b2e52ed5a2f7ca79194d9ef/01d767bc001665a0816cb3783a5f5b156c096fc1b651304ee6a6350b7be75991" :answer/id #uuid "067751b8-d9b0-5947-868e-d67de8882ded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94609/ma-source-field/7c3d1af2662a8686d500207febe06092bfdcfbd03b2e52ed5a2f7ca79194d9ef/382d2dbb372319e9327163bd6a1425a2