q-95216" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 4}(R),$ the vector space of all $6\\times 4$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{6\\times 4}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{6\\times 4}(R))=6\\cdot 4=24.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95216/ma-source-field/48a7173c34e06d46724806bd64a495489be35819ffdf359a0b0b785fb7ab131e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186172634 :question/answer-fields 17592186171399] {:db/id "q-96040/ma-source-field/f30f5fbf17f70bb01ef9b475554c2ad1e4ea2f1df9ef5e44f745e9aecc176bde/0fdd60dcf741ceb1e2dac3ec27e297adaa5541b6cf77020aaa5bb3f30b2ceeb4" :answer/id #uuid "82c1c1cb-051e-5f0a-9b5d-0cf75a3feb29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f:Q\\to X" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96040/ma-source-field/f30f5fbf17f70bb01ef9b475554c2ad1e4ea2f1df9ef5e44f745e9aecc176bde/9b826e1cfd2189bfcbc4d5d7ef103cca637ee61bd6d8eb79bdec4ad4e365ab99" :answer/id #uuid "e098e76f-5a82-5b93-8abb-179c4f6ed79b" :answer/type :answer.type/m